\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latin American stocks rise on Japan stimulus optimism\b0\par\par\uc2 518 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juli 2016\par 00:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Updates prices)\par     By Bruno Federowski\par     SAO PAULO, July 11 (Reuters) - Latin American stocks gained\par on Monday amid prospects of a fresh stimulus package in Japan,\par while the Brazilian real slipped after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Japanese Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shinzo Abe\f28 \uc2 \f2  said he ordered a new\par round of fiscal stimulus measures after his coalition emerged\par victorious from parliamentary elections, steering investors\par toward higher-risk assets. \par     His comments added to a bout of bullish sentiment triggered\par by stronger-than-expected U.S. jobs data published last Friday.\par  \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 MSCI\f28 \uc2 \f2 's benchmark EM index climbed more than 2\par percent to its highest in 2-1/2 months, while emerging market\par dollar bond yield spreads were at the tightest levels in almost\par a year.  \par     "This resilience of EM bonds can also be explained by the\par fact that the fixed-income market is facing what has become a\par structural problem: the negative rates in Europe and Japan,"\par Regis Chatellier, EM credit strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Societe Generale\f28 \uc2 \f2 , told\par clients.\par     "In this difficult environment, investors have to find a\par source of yield somewhere, and emerging markets clearly appear\par as a valid alternative for this," he said.\par     Chatellier said he upped his recommendation on emerging\par market sovereign debt to "neutral," with big overweight\par positions in Colombia and Argentina.\par     But the Brazilian real dropped 0.47 percent as the\par country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  once again \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after staying put on Friday.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's benchmark Bovespa stock index rose 1.54\par percent, supported by shares of state-controlled oil company\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petr\u243\'00\'F3leo Brasileiro SA\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     Analysts at Ita\u250\'00\'FA BBA improved its recommendation for\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petrobras\f28 \uc2 \f2 , as the company is known, to "outperform" and\par increased their price target to 14 reais from 9 reais.\par     "Short- and medium-term challenges remain, but we believe\par they have already been mapped out by the market," Ita\u250\'00\'FA BBA\par analyst Diego Mendes wrote in a report.\par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 2134 GMT:\par  Stock indexes               Latest          Daily   YTD pct\par                                                pct    change\par                                             change  \par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 MSCI\f28 \uc2 \f2  Emerging Markets            846.73      2.16      6.62\par                                                     \par  MSCI LatAm                     2,297.68      1.69     25.57\par  Brazil Bovespa                53,960.11      1.54     24.48\par  Mexico IPC                    46,177.61      0.95      7.45\par  Chile IPSA                     4,034.24      0.23      9.62\par  Chile IGPA                    19,944.27      0.23      9.88\par  Argentina MerVal              14,977.30      1.95     28.28\par  Colombia IGBC                  9,682.69      0.73     13.28\par  Venezuela IBC                 11,881.62      0.61    -18.55\par                                                       