\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Brazil cenbank nominee vows to cut inflation to target rate\b0\par\par\uc2 447 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juni 2016\par 20:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds senate committee approving his nomination)               \par \par \uc2 By Alonso Soto               \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA, June 7 (Reuters) - Brazil's nominated \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Ilan Goldfajn vowed on Tuesday to keep a lid on price pressures as part of the interim government's efforts to rebuild the "tripod" policy framework of fiscal discipline, low inflation and a free exchange rate.               \par \par \uc2 Goldfajn, former chief economist at lender \uc2 Itau Unibanco\uc2 , was speaking to the Senate's economic affairs committee for his confirmation hearing. The committee approved his nomination, but  the Senate must still ratify the decision.               \par \par \uc2 He said the bank's current chief, \uc2 Alexandre Tombini\uc2 , will lead the decision on interest rates on Wednesday, signaling he will not take part in the two-day rate-setting meeting that starts later on Tuesday.               \par \par \uc2 Interim President \uc2 Michel Temer\uc2 , who replaced President Dilma Rousseff while she stands trial for allegedly doctoring fiscal accounts, has picked market-friendly economists and executives for key posts in a bid to regain investors' confidence.               \par \par \uc2 Temer, who was Rousseff's vice president, has pledged to abandon years of state \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for more business-friendly policies to end \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's worst recession in decades.               \par \par \uc2 Goldfajn, who was the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's director of economic policy between 2000 and 2003, said he will seek to "fully" comply with the bank's objective to bring inflation down to the 4.5 percent center of the official target range. The bank has overshot the target center for the past five years.               \par \par \uc2 He twice defended a floating exchange rate regime in his speech, helping boost the country's real \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by 0.67 percent to 3.46 reais per dollar.               \par \par \uc2 Many traders saw the comments as a sign he would let the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthen past 3.50 per U.S. dollar, a level that triggered \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .               \par \par \uc2 The Israeli-born economist said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  should not be used as an instrument to bring down inflation. Recently, the government has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen the real to soften inflation - a move which many analysts said conflicted with the tripod policy framework of the past decade.               \par \par \uc2 "I believe there is consensus that we need to rebuild as soon as possible the tripod framework ... that brought social and economic gains to Brazil in the recent past," Goldfajn said.               \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is widely expected to keep its benchmark Selic rate at a near 10-year high of 14.25 percent on Wednesday as inflation remains well above target.               \par \par \uc2 Brazil's inflation has eased from 12-year highs earlier this year but is not expected to reach 5 percent until next year.               \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-6-7T19:33:00.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160607ec6701b87\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
