\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  weaken as Fed policy minutes awaited\b0\par\par\uc2 514 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 2016\par 23:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Updates with final prices)\par     By Bruno Federowski\par     SAO PAULO, May 18 (Reuters) - Most Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par weakened on Wednesday amid growing expectations that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal\par Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  would increase U.S. interest rates relatively soon,\par drawing investment flows away from emerging market assets.\par     Quickening inflation data and comments by Fed policymakers\par had revived those bets ahead of the release on Wednesday of the\par minutes of the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's most recent policy meeting.\par     Nevertheless, interest rates futures contracts indicate\par traders remain skeptical about the two to three rate hikes this\par year eyed by some officials at the Fed. \par     "The minutes are likely to reinforce a clear bias to\par normalization with discussions surrounding the timing of the\par next hike," Scotiabank strategists wrote in a client note.\par     The Brazilian real fell by more than 2 percent,\par underperforming its regional peers after the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold $1 billion in reverse \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swaps, which correspond\par to dollar purchases in futures markets.\par     The bank, which has bolstered its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy as\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's political crisis triggered \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  volatility, had\par remained on the sidelines for the last three days.\par     Brazil's benchmark Bovespa stock index seesawed as\par U.S. shares turned positive in early trading, but a drop in\par shares of Cielo SA weighed on the index.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banco Santander Brasil SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  cut its recommendation\par for the stock to "underperform," citing high stock prices and\par regulatory concerns. Shares of Eletrobras ,\par which are not part of the index, fell over 2 percent.\par     The state-controlled electricity holding company's American\par Depository Receipts will be delisted after it missed a\par May 18 deadline to deliver its 20-F form, a requirement for\par foreign issuers listed in the United States. \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Centrais El\u233\'00\'E9tricas Brasileiras SA\f28 \uc2 \f2 , as the company is\par formally known, has said the documents were delayed by an\par internal investigation that is analyzing potential financial\par losses from a graft scheme involving local construction firms.\par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 2100 GMT:\par     \par  Stock indexes                     Latest        Daily  YTD pct\par                                                    pct   change\par                                                 change  \par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 MSCI\f28 \uc2 \f2  Emerging Markets                 794.22    -0.93     0.01\par  MSCI LatAm                          2,110.98    -1.42    15.37\par  Brazil Bovespa                     50,561.70    -0.55    16.64\par  Mexico IPC                         45,551.20    -0.70     5.99\par  Chile IPSA                          3,966.45    -0.25     7.78\par  Chile IGPA                         19,510.57    -0.21     7.49\par  Argentina MerVal                   12,829.93    -1.52     9.89\par  Colombia IGBC                       9,866.82    -1.22    15.44\par  Venezuela IBC                      15,014.40     4.09     