\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latin American shares gain as oil hits 6-month high\b0\par\par\uc2 452 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 2016\par 23:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Updates prices)\par     BRASILIA, May 16 (Reuters) - Latin American stocks rose on\par Monday as oil prices hit a six-month high and other commodities\par also gained, while investors waited for greater clarity on the\par next steps of Brazil's interim president.\par     The MSCI Latin American stock index gained\par 0.21 percent as benchmark indexes in Brazil, Mexico and Colombia\par advanced. Non-voting shares in Brazil's state-run oil producer\par Petroleo Brasileiro SA rose more than 3 percent,\par boosted by a 3 percent increase in oil prices.\par     Oil hit six-month highs on Monday on worries about global\par supply outages and as long-time bear \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2  sounded more\par positive on the market.\par     Crude futures have rallied for most of the past two weeks\par from a combination of Nigerian, Venezuelan and other outages,\par declining U.S. production and virtually frozen inflows of\par Canadian crude after wildfires in Alberta's oil sands region.\par     In \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, the Brazilian real erased some\par of Friday's losses and outperformed its peers with an increase\par of 0.56 percent against the U.S. dollar.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stayed clear from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remained at 3.50 per dollar.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Finance Minister Henrique Meirelles postponed to\par Tuesday the announcement of the next \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief,\par Treasury secretary and other members of the economic team. \par     Meirelles, a former \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief, promised to unveil\par tough measures to close a widening fiscal gap that cost Brazil\par its coveted investment grade rating last year. \par     In Mexico, the IPC stock index gained 0.97 percent,\par but the peso weakened 0.40 percent to 18.23 pesos per dollar. \par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 :\par     \par  Stock indexes                             daily %     YTD %\par                                Latest       change    change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 MSCI\f28 \uc2 \f2  Emerging Markets            797.86      0.22      0.24\par                                                     \par  MSCI LatAm                      2162.26      0.21     17.92\par                                                     \par  Brazil Bovespa                 51843.14      0.08     19.60\par                                                     \par  Mexico IPC                     45841.05      0.97      6.66\par                                                     \par  Chile IPSA                      3987.06     -0.39      8.34\par                                                     \par  Chile IGPA                     19597.12     -0.33      7.96\par                                                     \par  Argentina MerVal               13183.48      0.47     12.92\par                                                     \par  Colombia IGBC                  10069.57      0.76     17.81\par                                                     \par  Venezuela IBC                  15375.59     -0.04      5.40\par                                                     \par                                                             \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                                 daily %     YTD %\par                                             change    change\par                                   Latest            \par  Brazil real                      3.5025      0.56     13.04\par                                                     \par  Mexico peso                     18.2335     -0.40     -5.50\par                                                     \par  Chile peso                          694     -0.46      2.26\par                                                     \par  Colombia peso                    3027.1     -1.19      4.70\par  Peru sol                         3.3299      0.18      2.53\par                                                     \par  Argentina peso (interbank)      14.1350      0.16     -8.15\par                                                     \par  Argentina peso (parallel)         14.63      0.00     -2.46\par                                                     \par  \par  (Reporting by Silvio Cascione; Editing by Paul Simao and Dan\par Grebler)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-5-16T22:11:06.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160516ec5g024xk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
