\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Thin trading in LatAm markets after U.S. jobs report\b0\par\par\uc2 471 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Mai 2016\par 18:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BRASILIA, May 6 (Reuters) - Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and\par stocks traded thinly on Friday after weaker-than-expected jobs\par numbers in the U.S. reduced expectations of interest rate hikes\par by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  this year. \par     The broader MSCI Latin American stock index,\par the Brazil's Bovespa stock index and the Mexican stock\par index all fell slightly, with no clear trend.\par     Most \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were up against the U.S., with the exception\par of the Colombian peso. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stayed clear\par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets for a third\par consecutive day as the real was little changed. \par     "The market is moving laterally, sticking to this range\par between 3.50 and 3.55 reais per dollar as it waits for a new\par economic team to take office next week," said Ricardo Silva,\par head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trading at Brazilian brokerage Correparti,\par referring to the likely replacement of President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dilma Rousseff\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par by Vice-President Michel Temer next week. \par     Stocks dipped worldwide after data showed U.S. non-farm\par payrolls increased by 160,000 jobs last month, far below the\par 202,000 economists polled by Reuters had forecast on average.\par The number cast doubts on whether the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  will raise\par interest rates before the end of the year. \par     Economic data also showed Brazil's inflation slowing less\par than expected last month. Yields on Brazilian interest rate\par futures <0#2DIJ:> rose as traders saw a smaller likelihood of\par interest rate cuts by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at its next meeting in\par June. \par     In equities markets, shares of Mexican home builder\par Desarrolladora Homex SAB de CV fell more than 5\par percent after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par notified it about a planned enforcement action related to\par fraudulent real estate sales. \par         \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1553 GMT:\par         \par  Stock                        Latest    daily %  YTD %\par    indexes                              change   change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 MSCI\f28 \uc2 \f2  Emerging Markets        804.03    -0.67    1.93\par                                                  \par  MSCI LatAm                   2158.70   -0.13    18.13\par                                                  \par  Brazil Bovespa               51553.74  -0.23    18.92\par  Mexico IPC                   45065.64  -0.18    4.86\par  Chile IPSA                   4001.49   -0.32    8.73\par  Chile IGPA                   19681.58  -0.27    8.43\par  Argentina MerVal             13476.38  0.96     15.43\par  Colombia IGBC                9600.49   0.19     12.32\par  Venezuela IBC                15382.15  0.09     5.44\par                                                  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                    Latest    daily %  YTD %\par                                         change   change\par  Brazil real                  3.5270    0.35     11.91\par  Mexico peso                  17.9060   -