\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  official expects  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  to reduce  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 268 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 April 2016\par 00:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds background and further comments from official, paragraphs 4-7)               \par \par \uc2 By Patricia Duarte               \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA, April 19 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  less in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as it expects volatility to ease in coming days after lawmakers voted to impeach President \uc2 Dilma Rousseff\uc2 , a senior government official told Reuters on Tuesday.               \par \par \uc2 "Given the market today, the work will be done with a lighter hand," said the official who asked not to be named because he was not allowed to speak publicly. "If you \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market more than necessary, then you end up weighing too much."               \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stayed away from the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday after weeks of heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the real from strengthening further ahead of last Sunday's controversial impeachment vote.               \par \par \uc2 Markets cheered the overwhelming vote in the lower house of Congress against Rousseff, who would be suspended from office for up to 6 months if the Senate ratifies that vote in early May. She would be replaced by Vice-President Michel Temer, who is expected to implement more market-friendly policies to pull the economy out of its worst recession in over a century.               \par \par \uc2 The official said he expects less \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility in coming days after the initial impeachment vote.               \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has used reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps to purchase more than $29 billion worth of future dollars this month, which has mitigated the effect of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rally prompted by investor bets on the ouster of Rousseff.               \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-4-19T23:12:22.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160419ec4j025pb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
