\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil stocks jump to 10-month high on impeachment bets\b0\par\par\uc2 545 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 April 2016\par 22:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Adds Argentina index jumps 4.5 percent, peso rises on U.S.\par appeals court decision on debt; updates prices)\par     By Bruno Federowski\par     SAO PAULO, April 13 (Reuters) - Brazilian stocks hit their\par highest level in nearly 10 months on Wednesday amid expectations\par of President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dilma Rousseff\f28 \uc2 \f2 's ouster, but the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par was dented by the heightened \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's lower house will vote on Sunday on whether to allow\par impeachment proceedings against the leftist president to advance\par to a Senate vote.\par     Lawmakers' support for the survival of her government seemed\par to dwindle after the Progressive Party (PP) officially left the\par administration on Tuesday. The party's leader in the lower house\par said a majority of its 49 deputies supported impeachment.\par  \par     Brazil's stocks and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have rallied for weeks as many\par traders bet impeachment could rekindle trust in the embattled\par economy and ease the approval of austerity measures in Congress.\par     Shares of state-controlled firms such as oil company\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petroleo Brasileiro SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  and lender \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banco do Brasil SA\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par  rose, driving the benchmark Bovespa stock index\par  to jump 3.2 percent to its highest since late June 2015.\par     But the Brazilian real pared most of its gains,\par closing up just 0.4 percent, after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped up\par its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The bank bought $3.15 billion in the markets through reverse\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swaps on Wednesday following an unprecedented $8\par billion purchase the day before.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas\f28 \uc2 \f2  strategists praised the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , saying the\par real had appreciated beyond what was warranted by macroeconomic\par fundamentals.\par     Elsewhere in the region, Argentina's MerVal stock index\par  jumped 4.5 percent, and the peso rose a two-month high,\par after a U.S. appeals court lifted injunctions which should allow\par the country to pay off some debts in a years-long litigation\par stemming from its 2002 default. \par     Mexico's IPC stock index gained 0.7 percent while\par Chile's IPSA rose 0.45 percent, boosted by upbeat\par Chinese trade data which showed exports returned to growth for\par the first time in nine months, offering hope about the world's\par second-biggest economy. \par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1959 GMT:\par  Stock indexes                             daily %     YTD %\par                                Latest       change    change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 MSCI\f28 \uc2 \f2  Emerging Markets            845.03       1.7      4.63\par                                                     \par  MSCI LatAm                      2243.44      2.32     19.83\par                                                     \par  Brazil Bovespa                 53190.69      2.29     22.70\par                                                     \par  Mexico IPC                     45405.75       0.7      5.65\par                                                     \par  Chile IPSA                      3957.24      0.09      7.53\par                                                     \par  Chile IGPA                     19394.81      0.11      6.85\par                                                     \par  Argentina MerVal               13256.31      4.43     13.54\par                                                     \par  Colombia IGBC                  10135.17      0.57     18.58\par                                                     \par  Venezuela IBC                  15659.55       2.6      7.34\par                                                     \par                                                             \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                                 daily %     YTD %\par                                             change    change\par                                   Latest            \par  Brazil real                      3.4775      0.41     11.90\par                                                     \par  Mexico peso                     17.4590      0.13     -1.33\par                                                     \par  Chile peso                        670.2      0.45      5.57\par                                                     \par  Colombia peso                    3006.2      0.32      5.15\par                                                     \par  Peru sol                         3.2629     -0.02      4.43\par                                                     \par  Argentina peso (interbank)      14.3900      0.55    -10.84\par                                                     \par  Argentina peso (parallel)         14.87      0.93     -4.20\par                                                     \par  \par  (Reporting by Bruno Federowski; additional reporting by Paula\par Arend Laier, editing by G Crosse and G