\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil currency \highlight\uc2  firms on limited cenbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 478 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2016\par 23:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Updates prices in table)\par     By Bruno Federowski and Paula Arend Laier\par     SAO PAULO, March 22 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real\par strengthened 0.26 percent on Tuesday as traders bet the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will stick to a strategy of limited action to slow the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent rally.\par     For a second straight day, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold only some\par of the reverse \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swaps -  equivalent to buying U.S.\par dollars in the futures market - it had offered.\par     The bank had not conducted reverse \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swap sales in\par three years before Monday, leading some to speculate that the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was meant to keep the real weaker than a certain\par level in order to boost exports.\par     But the bank only sold 15,500 contracts out of the 34,500\par offered in the last two sessions, suggesting it could allow the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to keep strengthening as long as it does so slowly.\par     Brazil's stocks and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have rallied over the last\par month as traders bet that growing chances of political change\par could boost investor confidence in the ailing Brazilian economy.\par     The country's benchmark stock index fell 0.32 percent on\par Tuesday, hit by weakness in financial shares. Stocks of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petroleo\par Brasileiro SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  seesawed after the state-controlled oil\par company reported a record quarterly loss, but ended the session\par up 0.62 percent. \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petrobras\f28 \uc2 \f2 , as the company is known, booked a large writedown\par of oil-related assets due to slumping oil prices. However, some\par analysts struck an upbeat tone, citing solid operating profit\par and cash flow.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2  analysts upgraded their recommendation for\par the company's New York-listed shares to "equal-weight" from\par "underweight," saying higher appetite for Brazilian assets and\par better sentiment in oil markets should support the stock.\par     In Mexico, the peso gained 0.42 percent, helped by stable\par oil prices. The IPC stock index added 0.33 percent. \par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 2230 GMT:\par  Stock indexes               Latest          Daily   YTD pct\par                                                pct    change\par                                             change  \par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 MSCI\f28 \uc2 \f2  Emerging Markets            830.51      0.17      4.58\par                                                     \par  MSCI LatAm                     2,160.60      0.38     18.08\par                                                     \par  Brazil Bovespa                51,010.19     -0.32     17.67\par  Mexico IPC                    45,632.28      0.33      6.18\par  Chile IPSA                     3,950.96     -0.44      7.36\par  Chile IGPA                    19,335.50     -0.43      6.52\par  Argentina MerVal              12,926.33     -0.08     10.72\par  Colombia IGBC                  9,743.39      0.45     13.99\par                                                             \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                        Latest     Daily   YTD pct\par                                                pct    change\par                                             change  \par  Brazil real                      3.6008      0.26       N/A\par  Mexico peso                      17.327      0.42     -0.56\par  Chile peso                        673.4      0.46      5.39\par  Colombia peso                     3,029      1.43      4.67\par  Peru sol                         3.4071      0.06      0.20\par  \par  (Reporting by Bruno Federowski and Paula Arend Laier; Editing\par by Andrea Ricci and Chris Reese)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-3-22T23:48:34.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160322ec3m027v1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
