\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil real, stocks rally on news Rousseff implicated in probe\b0\par\par\uc2 480 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2016\par 22:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Updates prices)\par     By Bruno Federowski\par     SAO PAULO, March 3 (Reuters) - Brazil's stocks jumped by the\par most in six years and the real \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also rallied on Thursday\par on news that bolstered the case to impeach President Dilma\par Rousseff and bets the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could take longer to cut\par interest rates.\par     The Brazilian stock market rose 5.4 percent, its\par largest one-day rally since October 2009, also helped by\par favorable corporate news. The real rose 2.4 percent, its\par biggest jump in nearly five months, outperforming regional\par peers.\par     According to local media, Brazilian ruling party senator\par Delcidio do Amaral agreed to a plea bargain implicating Rousseff\par and her predecessor Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva in a graft\par scandal. Amaral declined to confirm the report. \par     Analysts said the scandal bolsters the case for Rousseff's\par impeachment, encouraging investors who blame her Worker Party's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventionist\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policies for driving \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  into what could be\par its deepest recession on record. \par     "The market is betting Rousseff will not finish her\par mandate," said Pedro Tuesta, an economist with 4Cast in\par Washington D.C.\par     The real, which closed at a three-month high of 3.7977 per\par dollar, was supported by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's split decision to\par keep benchmark rates at 14.25 percent after markets closed on\par Wednesday. \par     The split vote, with two of the eight members voting for a\par 50-basis-points increase, led traders to trim bets on a rate cut\par later this year or early next year. Inflation has been running\par at double-digits, way above the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's target range.\par     Stock markets across the region also rose, with Mexico's IPC\par stock index hitting its highest in more than three\par months, following a return of risk appetite and a recovery in\par commodity prices.\par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 2106 GMT:\par  Stock indexes                             daily %     YTD %\par                                Latest       change    change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 MSCI\f28 \uc2 \f2  Emerging Markets            781.34      1.59     -3.15\par                                                     \par  MSCI LatAm                      1970.49      3.72      3.82\par                                                     \par  Brazil Bovespa                 47323.80      5.41      9.17\par                                                     \par  Mexico IPC                     44742.22      0.28      4.11\par                                                     \par  Chile IPSA                      3817.39      1.34      3.73\par                                                     \par  Chile IGPA                     18707.96      1.38      3.07\par                                                     \par  Argentina MerVal               13327.87       0.8     14.16\par                                                     \par  Colombia IGBC                   9548.46      0.94     11.71\par                                                     \par  Venezuela IBC                  16267.34      0.11     11.51\par                                                     \par                                    