\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Aims to Stimulate Growth Without Stoking Inflation, Minister Says\b0\par\par\uc2 By Paulo Trevisani   \par \uc2 530 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 2016\par 00:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \par \par \uc2 \f2 BRAS\u205\'00\'CDLIA--Brazil's government is working on a plan to alleviate the country's deep recession without further destabilizing its finances or stoking already high inflation, a cabinet member said Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Details of the plan are still under discussion but could be announced as soon as next week, President \uc2 Dilma Rousseff\uc2 's spokesman, Social Communication Minister Edinho Silva, told The Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 "The economy needs stimulus, with responsibility," Mr. Silva said. "It is necessary to fight unemployment."\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, the government said Brazil lost 1.5 million jobs in 2015, the most since 1992.\par \par \uc2 Latin America's largest economy shrank by 3.7% last year, according to economists surveyed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Tax revenue fell in line with the recession, which in turn pushed Brazil's budget deficit to 9.3% of gross domestic product as of November. December data will be released next week, and analysts expect the deficit to increase.\par \par \uc2 The economic slowdown, however, didn't stop prices from rising at a 10.7% annual pace, more than double the official target.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Silva said the measures under consideration shouldn't stoke inflation because price increases have been driven by government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation. Government-controlled prices were increased sharply last year.\par \par \uc2 "Brazil's inflation isn't caused by excessive demand," he said. "Every economist agrees on that."\par \par \uc2 Fixing the economic problems is an uphill battle, as a deeply unpopular Ms. Rousseff battles impeachment procedures in a hostile Congress. Ms. Rousseff has said her past and present behavior vouch for her honesty and her commitment to the law.\par \par \uc2 The executive branch has been trying for months to put together a plan to boost the economy, mainly by extending credit through state banks, but a comprehensive stimulus program has yet to be rolled out.\par \par \uc2 Last year's toxic political environment made it almost impossible to pass legislation aimed at reducing costs and increasing taxes. Former Finance Minister Joaquim Levy tried to persuade lawmakers to support austerity, but most of his measures got stuck in political gridlock. In December, Ms. Rousseff named then Planning Minister \uc2 Nelson Barbosa\uc2  to be the new finance minister. Mr. Barbosa has promised to keep austerity as a priority.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Silva also said that market rumors of government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week weren't true.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Wednesday that it would keep its Selic short-term rate unchanged at 14.25%, despite signaling in recent weeks that it could raise interest rates. Market watchers noted \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President \uc2 Alexandre Tombini\uc2  had met with Ms. Rousseff on Monday, two days before the rate decision.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Silva said the meeting was between Mr. Barbosa and Ms. Rousseff to discuss the finance minister's participation in the \uc2 World Economic Forum\uc2  in Davos, Switzerland. Mr. Tombini, who didn't go to the forum, was invited to give some input, Mr. Silva said.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Rousseff has repeatedly said she doesn't interfere with monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 Write to Paulo Trevisani at paulo.trevisani@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 22, 2016 18:53 ET (23:53 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160122ec1m0050n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
