\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil real bucks Latam losses as  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  acts\b0\par\par\uc2 421 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 November 2015\par 19:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SAO PAULO, Nov 5 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real strengthened\par more than 0.5 percent on Thursday, outperforming Latin American\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to provide liquidity\par to the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold as much as $500 million on the\par spot market with agreements to repurchase those dollars on Jan.\par 4 and April 4 of next year. It was the second time this week the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  through these so-called repo\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par     The bank has been increasing its offering of dollars, as it\par usually does at the end of the year, when dollars may be scarce\par as more Brazilians vacation abroad and foreign companies send\par more profits to their headquarters.\par     The real last traded at 3.78 per dollar, 0.5 percent\par stronger from Wednesday's close after gaining as much as 0.8\par percent earlier.\par     "It seems that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is sending a clear message\par to the market with those repo auctions that it is not\par comfortable with a real weaker than 3.8 per dollar," said\par Jefferson Luiz Rugik, a trader with Correparti brokerage in\par Brazil.\par     Other Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened for a second\par consecutive day after U.S. Federal Reserve Chair \f28 \uc2 \f2 Janet Yellen\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par signaled a growing chance that U.S. interest rates may go up in\par December, potentially reducing the allure of emerging-market\par assets.\par \par     Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1820 GMT:\par     \par  Stock indexes                 Latest       Daily  YTD pct\par                                               pct   change\par                                            change  \par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 MSCI\f28 \uc2 \f2  Emerging Markets            863.81     -0.5    -9.22\par                                                    \par  MSCI LatAm                     2,073.91     0.17   -24.09\par  Brazil Bovespa                47,911.74     0.42    -4.19\par  Mexico IPC                    45,351.46    -0.05     5.11\par  Chile IPSA                     3,860.04    -0.15     0.24\par  Chile IGPA                    18,947.81    -0.13     0.41\par  Argentina MerVal              12,890.19     0.71    50.25\par  Colombia IGBC                  9,243.87     0.39   -20.55\par  Venezuela IBC                 11,935.46    -0.05   209.31\par                                                           \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                        Latest    Daily  YTD pct\par                                               pct   change\par                                            change  \par  Brazil real                      3.7790     0.45   -29.68\par  Mexico peso                     16.6102    -0.41   -11.24\par  Chile peso                        694.5    -0.50   -12.69\par  Colombia peso                     2,857    -0.75   -16.42\par  Peru sol                         3.3041    -0.24    -9.84\par  Argentina peso (interbank)       9.5775    -0.08   -10.73\par                           