\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's real extends slide despite  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 507 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 2015\par 16:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SAO PAULO, Sept 29 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's real extended its\par decline into a third session on Tuesday as traders, concerned\par about the outlook for commodities prices and local growth,\par shrugged off the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's efforts to boost the battered\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the region were little changed, while\par stocks moved slightly higher.\par     The real strengthened at the open following the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's announcement after Monday's close that it would sell up\par to $2 billion in the spot market on Tuesday with repurchase\par agreements and hold an unscheduled \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swap auction.\par     Still, the real remained near its weakest level on record,\par hovering near 4.13 per dollar. \par     "It seems that the Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market is no longer\par accepting 'more of the same' when it comes to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par auctions and is testing the bank for something stronger,"\par Jefferson Luiz Rugik, a trader with Brazilian brokerage\par Correparti, wrote in a client note.\par     Investors have been betting heavily against the real in the\par futures market, given that the economy is in recession,\par inflation exceeds 9 percent, government finances have\par deteriorated sharply and a ratings agency has lowered Brazil's\par debt to "junk" status.\par     In addition, disappointing economic data from top trade\par partner China has weighed on the price of local commodity\par exports, putting an additional drag on the real, which has lost\par nearly 36 percent of its value against the dollar this year.\par     Elsewhere, the Colombian and Mexican pesos  both\par remained nearly flat, while the Chilean peso advanced\par slightly on higher prices for copper, the country's main\par export.\par     In equities markets, Brazil's Bovespa stock index \par looked set to snap a seven-session slump, led by shares of the\par most widely traded banking and commodities companies, such as\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banco Bradesco SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  and state-run oil producer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petroleo\par Brasileiro SA\f28 \uc2 \f2 , or \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petrobras\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     Finance Minister Joaquim Levy said on Tuesday that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petrobras\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par was taking the right steps to shore up its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the\par wake of a massive corruption investigation.    \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1400 GMT:\par     \par  Stock indexes                        daily %    YTD %\par                              Latest    change   change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets        775.82    -0.74   -18.27\par                                                \par  MSCI LatAm                  1829.72    -0.75   -32.41\par                                                \par  Brazil Bovespa           44292.6659     0.76   -11.43\par                                    4           \par  Mexico IPC                 42033.68     0.33    -2.58\par                                                \par  Chile IPSA                  3662.79     0.27    -4.89\par                                   