\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's real finds support in cenbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 481 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 2015\par 19:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SAO PAULO, Sept 25 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real stabilized\par on Friday following a session marked by extreme volatility as\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped up market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to soothe\par jittery investors.\par     Other Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were mixed, while most of\par the region's stock markets were little changed.\par     The real  fluctuated in early trading but\par settled in positive territory by the afternoon. \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strengthened about 0.7 percent to 3.96 per\par dollar, pushing it further away from the important 4 per dollar\par psychological threshold crossed on Tuesday.\par     The real hit its weakest level of all time earlier this\par week, sparking fears among investors that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's decline\par would continue apace.\par     Thursday's plunge was halted late in the session after\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alexandre Tombini\f28 \uc2 \f2  signaled that the bank had\par not ruled out selling part of the country's $371 billion foreign\par reserves to calm the market. \par     That calm returned during Friday's session, aided by another\par unscheduled swap auction held by the bank during morning\par trading.\par     "The market tests (the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) and it responds, and\par that repeats," said a trader who requested anonymity because he\par is not authorized to speak with journalists.\par     The real has been in a tailspin this year, weakening nearly\par 33 percent against the dollar as economic recession, lower\par commodities prices, expectations for higher interest rates in\par the United States and political turbulence at home rattle\par investors.\par     "We still didn't get any fundamental change in the negative\par picture for Brazil that would convince us that we have reached\par an inflexion point," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brown Brothers Harriman\f28 \uc2 \f2  analysts wrote in a\par client note on Friday.\par     Elsewhere in Latin America, Chile's peso slipped back\par following a sharp gain in the previous session, while Colombia's\par peso posted modest gains for the second straight day. \par \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1721 GMT:\par \par  Stock indexes                        daily %    YTD %\par                              Latest    change   change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets        789.71     0.51   -17.84\par                                                \par  MSCI LatAm                  1899.08     3.28   -32.59\par                                                \par  Brazil Bovespa           45160.3536    -0.29    -9.69\par                                    4           \par  Mexico IPC                 42582.97    -0.03    -1.30\par                                                \par  Chile IPSA                  3730.39     0.08    -3.13\par                                                \par  Chile IGPA                 18274.04     0.04    -3.16\par                                                \par  Argentina MerVal           9620.069     3.57    12.13\par                                                \par  Colombia IGBC               9293.48    -0.11   -20.12\par                                                \par  V