\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Respite for shares, Brazil's real after torrid week\b0\par\par\uc2 957 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 2015\par 12:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's real stabilises after c.bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vow\par     * EM stocks index sees second biggest weekly fall of year\par     * Pressure expected to return soon as Fed talks up rate\par hikes\par     * China stocks see small weekly fall by their standards\par \par     By Marc Jones\par     LONDON, Sept 25 (Reuters) - Alarm bells were ringing in\par emerging markets on Friday as shares trudged to their second\par worst week of the year and Brazil, Turkey and South Africa's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were all near record lows.\par     There was a consolation 0.7 percent rise on the day for\par MSCI's benchmark EM index but there were few cheers\par after a near 5 percent plunge this week which has taken its\par losses since April to an eyewatering 27 percent.\par     Brazil's real which has been battered particularly\par hard this week by mounting political and economic, was steadier\par after the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vowed to defend the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par with every weapon it has.\par     It had sparked a relief rally for South Africa's rand\par , Mexico's peso and Turkey's lira which have\par all hit all-time lows this week, but analysts suspected it would\par only prove temporary. \par     Particularly as Federal Reserve Chair \f28 \uc2 \f2 Janet Yellen\f28 \uc2 \f2  had said\par on Thursday the bank remained on track for its first interest\par rate hike in almost a decade later this year, something likely\par only to add to the EM world's woes..\par     Malaysia's ringgit and Indonesia's rupiah both\par fell to their lowest levels since the Asian financial crisis in\par 1998 in response, while the Singapore dollar stayed\par around a six-year trough on disappointing August output data.\par     "We have had a big emerging market sell-off this week\par especially because of contagion from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  where the real was\par in freefall before the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  yesterday from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said Bernd Berg at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Societe Generale\f28 \uc2 \f2  in London.    \par     "You saw a relief rally from this \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ... But we\par believe it is only going to be temporary because the situation\par is very negative for many emerging markets with China concerns,\par global concerns and uncertainty about the Fed."\par     Slumping commodity prices, the threat of rising U.S.\par interest rates, exacerbated in some cases by ugly national\par politics, have whipped up a near perfect storm for emerging\par markets this year.\par     The latest investment fund flow data showed the near-three\par month exodus from EM equities had extended and bond fund\par outflows reached a ninth straight week, although both were now\par more of a trickle than the gush of recent weeks. \par     China's shares fell 1.6 percent on Friday but it came after\par a remarkably quiet week by their recent standards. \par     A 1.5 percent rise meant central and eastern European stocks\par  were the day's best EM performers. However, for\par the week they have been some of the worst having been slammed\par over 5 percent by the crash in European car shares. \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Volkswagen\f28 \uc2 \f2  the company at the centre of a scandal over\par emissions tests cheating makes a large number of cars and parts\par in countries like Slovakia, the Czech Republic and Poland.\par          \par      Emerging Markets Prices from Reuters            \par  Equities                  Latest    Net Chg  % Chg  % Chg      \par      \par                                                      on year    \par        \par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2                \par  Emrg Mkt Indx    791.68    +6.00   +0.76  -17.22     \par        \par  Czech Rep            957.50    +6.28   +0.66   +1.14     \par        \par  Poland           2103.32   +20.37   +0.98   -9.18     \par        \par  Hungary           20797.41  +186.65   +0.91  +25.03     \par        \par  Romania           7187.91   +66.85   +0.94   +1.48     \par        \par  Greece              673.69    +5.87   +0.88  -18.46     \par        \par  Russia             786.46   +17.08   +2.22   -0.54     \par        \par  South Africa   45015.19   -46.86   -0.10   +2.38     \par         \par  Turkey          74610.20  -383.51   -0.51  -12.96     \par        \par  China             3091.81   -50.88   -1.62   -4.42     \par        \par  India           25863.50   +40.51   +0.16   -5.95     \par        \par             \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2               Latest    Prev    Local    Local       \par       \par                                    close   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     \par        \par                                            % change % change    \par        \par                                                     in 2015     \par       \par  Czech Rep      27.19     27.25   +0.24    +1.72      \par      \par  Poland          4.21      4.22   +0.20    +1.68      \par      \par  Hungary       314.39    313.69   -0.22    +0.66      \par      \par  Romania         4.41      4.42   +0.18    +1.59      \par      \par  Serbia        119.80    119.88   +0.07    +1.29      \p