\par\par \b \uc2 WRAPUP 3- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's beleaguered  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  rebounds after  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  threat\b0\par\par\uc2 568 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 2015\par 05:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 * Tombini does not rule out using reserves to boost \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Real rebounds, ends day below 4 per dollar               \par \par \uc2 * Unemployment rate rose in August to 5-year high               \par \par \uc2 By Alonso Soto and Walter Brandimarte               \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA/SAO PAULO, Sept 24 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rebounded strongly after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  vowed to defend it with every weapon it had, lifting the real off all times lows struck earlier on Thursday as investors fretted over the outlook for Latin America's largest economy.               \par \par \uc2 A growing political crisis that threatens to unseat President \uc2 Dilma Rousseff\uc2  and a deepening economic recession have dragged the Brazilian real to its weakest level since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was created in 1994.               \par \par \uc2 The real plumbed a new low of 4.248 to the U.S. dollar before bouncing back to end the day at 3.99 after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president \uc2 Alexandre Tombini\uc2  warned he was ready to use Brazil's $371 billion foreign reserves to calm the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if needed.               \par \par \uc2 "In this process, all instruments are available for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Tombini told an unscheduled press briefing. "Foreign reserves are an insurance that could and should be used."               \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rallied further, bringing its gains for the day to 3.0 percent, after the Treasury announced a program of daily debt auctions to provide liquidity to the local debt market.               \par \par \uc2 Brazil's main stock index also rebounded from earlier losses of as much as 2.0 percent and was up 0.2 percent in late afternoon trading.               \par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Joaquim Levy said late on Thursday that the program helped ease market jitters and reaffirmed that some foreign reserves could be sold to dampen volatility.               \par \par \uc2 Despite the pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Tombini reaffirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy of keeping interest rates at current levels for a prolonged period even as it raised its inflation forecast to well above its official target.               \par \par \uc2 In a quarterly report released on Thursday, the bank raised its 2016 inflation forecast to 5.3 percent from 4.8 percent.               \par \par \uc2 The worsening inflation outlook added the difficulties for policymakers, reluctant to raise interest rates during a worse-than-expected recession.               \par \par \uc2 Unemployment rose for an eighth straight month in August to the highest in over five years, although the increase was slightly smaller than markets expected, data showed on Thursday.               \par \par \uc2 Some economists warned the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  risked putting the real under more pressure if it does not raise interest rates at its next scheduled rate-setting meeting on Oct. 21.               \par \par \uc2 "If the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not hike in the next meeting, they will see another round of deterioration," Santander Securities strategist Sandro Sobral said in a note to clients.               \par \par \uc2 The crisis has fueled concern that another credit rating agency will follow \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  example and cut Brazil's rating to junk status, forcing many global funds to dump its bonds from their portfolios.               \par \par \uc2 Treasury\uc2  Chief Marcelo Saintive said on Thursday that Brazil would be able to avoid further credit rating downgrades if it succeeds in approving its latest fiscal package and showing long-term commitment to rebalancing its public accounts.               \par \par \uc2 Roussef's efforts to shore up deteriorating government finances will face a major test on Wednesday, when Brazil's Senate votes on whether to overturn presidential vetoes aimed at averting a surge in public spending.               \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-9-25T04:36:17.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150924eb9o00ixo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
