\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2  to Support Real\b0\par\par\uc2 553 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 September 2015\par 02:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 By Jeffrey T. Lewis\par \par \uc2 S\u195\'00\'C3O PAULO--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday to try to calm the country's volatile \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and prop up the real as the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued its slide against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The bank announced in the early afternoon auctions of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -swap contracts, which offer businesses a hedge against the weaker real, and auctions of dollar-repurchase agreements, which temporarily inject dollars into the market. Later Wednesday afternoon, the bank announced two more repurchase auctions.\par \par \uc2 The real had gone from 4.0150 to the dollar Wednesday morning to 4.1430 in the early afternoon, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet. The real exited active trading at 4.1325 to the dollar, after closing at 4.0450 on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The bank has used auctions of both instruments before to help support the real. In 2013, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  started a program of regular auctions of dollar-swap agreements. The bank stopped auctioning off new swap agreements earlier this year, but has been rolling over existing contracts. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also has auctioned off dollar-repurchase agreements on three occasions in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 The bank's announcement on Wednesday provided a brief boost for the real, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs to sell reais directly into the market to have a longer-lasting impact, said Luiz Carlos Baldan, a director of the Fourtrade brokerage in S\u227\'00\'E3o Paulo.\par \par \uc2 "They didn't do anything they haven't done before, that's why the dollar went back up again" shortly after the announcement, he said. "The bank should come in and sell dollars for real. If I sell my car, I don't ask for it back after just a few weeks, what's the point?"\par \par \uc2 The real has slumped in recent days, going from 3.9480 against the dollar at the close on Friday, to Wednesday's record lows against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The real was launched in 1994, replacing the previous \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as part of a plan to tame the country's out-of-control inflation.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lost about 70% of its value against the dollar in the past 12 months as the country's economy has struggled and a corruption scandal at state-controlled oil company \uc2 Petr\u243\'00\'F3leo Brasileiro SA\uc2  spread to implicate dozens of prominent politicians.\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Dilma Rousseff\uc2 , who hasn't been implicated in the scandal, has nevertheless seen her approval ratings plummet to less than 10%. Her efforts to shrink the government's budget deficit, and protect Brazil's investment-grade credit rating, have been complicated by her unpopularity, which has made it difficult to get her economic austerity program approved by Congress.\par \par \uc2 "The increasing financial sensitivity seems to be driven by the economy's political obstacles," said Alfredo Couti\u241\'00\'F1o, director for Latin America at \uc2 Moody's\uc2  Analytics. Ms. Rousseff "is facing strong resistance in Congress, and the risk of a political crisis is increasing."\par \par \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  downgraded Brazil's rating to junk status earlier this year, and analysts and traders expect other ratings companies to follow suit in coming days or weeks. Fitch and \uc2 Moody's\uc2  still give Brazil investment-grade ratings.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jeffrey T. Lewis at jeffrey.lewis@wsj.com.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 24-09-15 0023GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020150924eb9o0000l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
