\par\par \b \uc2 WRAPUP 1- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil currency \highlight\uc2  tumbles as crisis worries swamp  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Walter Brandimarte   \par \uc2 747 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 2015\par 22:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Sept 23 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real tumbled anew on Wednesday as fears of deteriorating government finances, a mounting political crisis and weaker Chinese demand for raw materials overwhelmed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As the real plunged to an all-time low of 4.14 per U.S. dollar, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  called extraordinary auctions to sell \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps and dollars with repurchase agreements, joining an array of emerging-market policymakers struggling to support their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Other Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also posted losses on concerns about the global economy, but the weakening of the real was magnified by fears that Brazilian lawmakers could reject a presidential veto needed to avert a surge in public expenditures.\par \par \uc2 Although Brazil's Congress early on Wednesday upheld key presidential vetoes to avert a surge in public expenditure, it postponed votes on two vetoes of bills that threatened to raise public expenditure in coming years.\par \par \uc2 Congress has not yet set a date for voting on the remaining vetoes.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  did little to support the real, which has now lost 35 percent of its value against the U.S. dollar so far this year. It initially trimmed losses but closed 2.3 percent lower at 4.1454 per dollar. Brazil's benchmark Bovespa stock index closed 2 percent lower.\par \par \uc2 "An \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  like that should be able to curb losses in the real, but volatility is too high," said Francisco Carvalho, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at BGC Liquidez, a brokerage in Brazil. "Investors are feeling lost and are running to the dollar."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  through swaps and dollar repurchase agreements have no impact on Brazil's $370 billion foreign reserves and Brazil is not considering tapping those reserves at the moment, a source at President \uc2 Dilma Rousseff\uc2 's economic team told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Brazil has not used its foreign reserves since the global economic crisis in 2009. A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said on Wednesday there were no U.S. dollar outflows from the country.\par \par \uc2 Repeated clashes between Brazilian President \uc2 Dilma Rousseff\uc2  and her wide-ranging alliance in Congress have exacerbated an economic slowdown and led \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  to strip Brazil of its investment-grade credit rating earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 The real's slump shows "no one is winning" in the current political impasse, the speaker of Brazil's lower house of Congress said.\par \par \uc2 President Rousseff's popularity has cratered since she was re-elected last year as the economy has stumbled into a severe recession, inflation has persisted and senior members of her Workers Party have been implicated in a snowballing corruption scandal involving the energy company \uc2 Petrobras\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, multiple interest rate hikes by \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at slowing inflation have boosted borrowing costs as well as consumer and company loan delinquencies, which remained at a two-year high in August, according to Thomson Reuters data.\par \par \uc2 While worries that the weakening Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could worsen inflation and may pressure the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  into further action, exporters of both commodities and industrial goods have expressed hope that the decline in the real will jumpstart foreign demand for their goods.\par \par \uc2 INCREASED \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  IN \b \highlight22\uc2 BRAZIL\b0 \highlight\uc2  AND MEXICO\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold 4,400 of the 20,000 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps it offered on Wednesday and called a similar sale for Thursday. It was the first time that Brazil sold swaps that were not aimed at rolling over expiring contracts since it ended its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -swap program in March.\par \par \uc2 The bank also announced it will sell as much as $2 billion on the spot market with repurchase dates set to July 5, 2016 and Sept. 2, 2016.\par \par \uc2 Mexican policymakers have also been fighting a slump in the peso, which has hit successive record lows this year lows, by selling $200 million a day to the market and offering $200 million more when the peso weakens by 1.0 percent.\par \par \uc2 While an increase in dollar sales in July briefly helped the peso stabilize, on Wednesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  broke past 17 per dollar to a one-month low.\par \par \uc2 Mexican policymakers have argued that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has little effect when the Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's losses are being driven by global concerns, but they are expected to extend the current auction program, which expires at the end of the month.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Walter Brandimarte and Bruno Federowski; Writing by Christian Plumb; Editing by Alan Crosby)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-9-26T20:44:37.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150923eb9n00qjl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
