\par\par \uc2 Foreign Exchange\par \b \uc2 Brazil's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Moves to Prop Up Real Amid Volatility\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jeffrey T. Lewis  and Paulo Trevisani   \par \uc2 870 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 2015\par 18:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones Top North American Equities Stories\par \uc2 DJTNAE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 S\u195\'00\'C3 O PAULO\u8212\'20\'14\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to try to calm the country's volatile \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and prop up the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real, which has been sliding {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/brazils-real-hits-two-decade-low-1442962341"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 against the dollar }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The bank announced in the early afternoon auctions of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -swap contracts, which offer businesses a hedge against the weaker real, and auctions of dollar-repurchase agreements, which temporarily inject dollars into the market. Later Wednesday afternoon, the bank announced two more repurchase auctions.\par \par \uc2 The real fell from 4.0150 to the dollar Wednesday morning to 4.1430 in the early afternoon, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet. The real exited active trading at 4.1325 to the dollar, after closing at 4.0450 on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The bank has used auctions of both instruments before to help support the real. In 2013, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  started a program of regular auctions of dollar-swap agreements. The bank stopped auctioning off new swap agreements earlier this year, but has been rolling over existing contracts. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also has auctioned off dollar-repurchase agreements on three occasions in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  use of repurchase and swap auctions provided a brief boost for the real, but it would need to sell reais directly into the market to have a longer-lasting impact, said Luiz Carlos Baldan, a director of the Fourtrade brokerage in S\u227\'00\'E3 o Paulo.\par \par \uc2 The bank's actions came after Brazil's Congress handed a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/brazil-congress-upholds-most-of-rousseffs-vetoes-on-extra-spending-1443006711"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rare victory to President Dilma Rousseff }}}\uc2  earlier in the day, sustaining presidential vetoes of spending bills that would have worsened the nation's fiscal problems at a time when the government is struggling to close a massive budget hole.\par \par \uc2 In a tense legislative session that started Tuesday night and continued into the wee hours of the morning, legislators voted to allow the president to kill expensive spending bills.\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers permitted 26 of Ms. Rousseff's 32 vetoes on bills that together would have added an estimated 127 billion reais ($31.5 billion) to government outlays.\par \par \uc2 The bills vetoed included ones granting hefty salary increases to government workers and tax breaks on fuel, among other things.\par \par \uc2 "It was a victory for the government accounts. If the vetoes were overturned, it would represent a big cost for this administration and future ones," said Cristiano Oliveira, chief economist at \uc2 Banco Fibra\uc2  in S\u227\'00\'E3 o Paulo.\par \par \uc2 Still, investors remain jittery about prospects for Latin America's largest economy. The real fell from 4.0150 to the dollar Wednesday morning to 4.1430 in the early afternoon, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet. The real exited active trading at 4.1325 to the dollar, after closing at 4.0450 on Tuesday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has slumped sharply in recent days, going from 3.9480 against the dollar at the close on Friday, to Wednesday's record lows against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The real was launched in 1994, replacing the previous \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as part of a plan to tame the country's out-of-control inflation.\par \par \uc2 "They didn't do anything they haven't done before, that's why the dollar went back up again" shortly after the announcement, he said. "The bank should come in and sell dollars for real. If I sell my car, I don't ask for it back after just a few weeks, what's the point?"\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lost about 70% of its value against the dollar in the past 12 months as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/brazil-sinks-into-recession-on-second-quarter-output-contraction-1440765489"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the country's economy has struggled }}}\uc2  and a corruption scandal at state-controlled oil company Petr\u243\'00\'F3 leo Brasileiro SA {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/brazilian-police-seek-to-question-former-president-in-petrobras-probe-1442008371"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spread to implicate dozens of prominent politicians }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ms. Rousseff, who hasn't been implicated in the scandal, has nevertheless seen her approval ratings plummet to less than 10%. Her efforts to shrink the government's budget deficit, and protect Brazil's investment-grade credit rating, have been complicated by her unpopularity, which has made it difficult to get her economic austerity program approved by Congress.\par \par \uc2 "The increasing financial sensitivity seems to be driven by the economy's political obstacles," said Alfredo Couti\u241\'00\'F1 o, director for Latin America at \uc2 Moody's\uc2  Analytics. Ms. Rousseff "is facing strong resistance in Congress, and the risk of a political crisis is increasing."\par \par \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  downgraded Brazil's rating to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/s-p-drops-brazil-debt-rating-one-notch-to-junk-1441838102"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 junk status }}}\uc2  earlier this year, and analysts and traders expect other ratings companies to follow suit in coming days or weeks. Fitch and \uc2 Moody's\uc2  still give Brazil investment-grade ratings.\par \par \uc2 While Wednesday's legislative action kept Brazil from digging itself an even deeper fiscal hole, Congress delayed decisions on a half-dozen other measures vetoed by Ms. Rousseff, including a bill that would increase some judiciary salaries by as much as 70%. The remaining bills would generate 47 billion reais ($11.5 billion) in additional spending through 2019, according to government estimates.\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers so far have shown little willingness to cooperate with Ms. Rousseff to pass deep program cuts and large tax increases needed to shore up Brazil's shaky finances.\par \par \uc2 Rogerio Jelmayer contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jeffrey T. Lewis at  and Paulo Trevisani at \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJTNAE1120150923eb9n0007g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
