\par\par \b \uc2 ADRs End Lower; Brazil Companies Decline\b0\par\par\uc2 561 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 2015\par 23:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 International stocks trading in New York closed lower on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The BNY Mellon index of American depositary receipts fell 0.76% to 124.62. The European index decreased 0.47% to 125.92, the Asian index dropped 0.95% to 129.48, the Latin American index fell 3.1% to 154.41 and the emerging markets index declined nearly 2% to 203.96.\par \par \uc2 Brazil-based companies with ADRs traded actively.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday to try to calm the country's volatile \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and prop up the real as the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued its slide against the dollar. Among Brazilian companies with ADRs, aircraft maker \uc2 Embraer SA\uc2  (ERJ, EMBR3.BR) declined 3.5% to $25.15, steelmaker \uc2 Companhia Siderurgica Nacional\uc2  (SID, CSNA3.BR) skidded 21% to 99 cents, \uc2 Gerdau SA\uc2  (GGB, GGBR3.BR, GGBR4.BR)--also a steelmaker--dropped 4.7% to $1.43, \uc2 Itau Unibanco Holding SA\uc2  (ITUB, ITUB3.BR, ITUB4.BR) fell 5.5% to $6.37, \uc2 Telefonica Brasil SA\uc2  (VIV, VIVT4.BR) decreased 5.3% to $9.14 and mobile-phone company \uc2 TIM Participacoes SA\uc2  (TSU, TIMP3.BR) declined 2.5% to $9.98.\par \par \uc2 Anheuser-Busch InBev NV\uc2  (BUD, ABI.BT) is buying Los Angeles-based brewery Golden Road Brewing, the beer giant's latest effort to tap into the growing demand for craft beers. The deal comes as \uc2 AB InBev\uc2  pursues beverage-maker \uc2 SABMiller PLC\uc2 , a bold move that, if successful, would create a brewing giant that would dominate much of the global beer market. \uc2 AB InBev\uc2 's ADRs rose 35 cents to $107.82.\par \par \uc2 Banco Santander SA\uc2  (SAN, SAN.MC) laid out financial targets for the next several years that were broadly in line with previous goals, disappointing some investors and analysts who had hoped for more ambitious objectives. ADRs of Europe's second largest bank by market value fell 2.8% to $5.28.\par \par \uc2 Banco Santander\uc2  (Brasil) SA (BSBR, SANB4.BR, SANB3.BR, SANB11.BR) is projecting an increase in its return on equity in the next year, despite the sluggish economic performance of Latin America's largest nation. The Brazilian unit of Spanish banking giant \uc2 Banco Santander\uc2  said it expects to reach an ROE of 15.6% in the next three years, up from 12.8% currently. ADRs of \uc2 Banco Santander\uc2  (Brasil) fell 5.45% to $3.12.\par \par \uc2 Diageo PLC\uc2  (DEO, DGE.LN) cautioned that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements will have a bigger impact than previously expected on its results for the 2016 financial year as higher prices deter customers in emerging markets. Still, the maker of \uc2 Johnnie Walker\uc2  whisky and Smirnoff vodka expects to complete the year with improved revenue and margins. The U.K.-based drinks group's ADRs fell nearly 1% to $105.36.\par \par \uc2 Total SA\uc2  (TOT, FP.FR) said it will pump less oil than previously forecasted in 2017 amid new cost cuts intended to protect its ability to pay investor dividends during a period of low oil prices, company officials said. The French oil giant lowered its output target for 2017 to an average 2.6 million barrels of oil equivalent a day from a previous target of 2.8 million. ADRs rose nine cents to $43.88.\par \par \uc2 Write to Tess Stynes at tess.stynes@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 September 23, 2015 17:46 ET (21:46 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150923eb9n0037o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
