\par\par \b \uc2 Brazilian Real Sinks, Shares Fall After \uc2 S&P\uc2  Sovereign Downgrade\b0\par\par\uc2 316 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 2015\par 22:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Jeffrey T. Lewis \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SAO PAULO--The Brazilian real sank against the dollar, and shares declined, after \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  cut Brazil's sovereign debt rating to junk status.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The Ibovespa stocks index fell 0.3% to 46503 points. The real exited active trading at 3.8652 to the dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet, after closing at 3.7942 on Wednesday. The real recovered some lost ground in the morning, after weakening to 3.90 in earlier trading, after \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The bank held two auctions of up to a total of $1.5 billion of dollar repurchase agreements. The bank held similar auctions on Tuesday. By injecting more dollars into Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the auctions drive down the price of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and help support the real.\par \par \uc2 The downgrade had been expected after the government on Aug. 31 sent Congress a budget proposal for 2016 that forecast a primary budget deficit, though the rapidness of \uc2 S&P\uc2 's decision surprised many. The primary budget balance is a measure of the government's ability to save and reduce debt, and the proposal was an indication that the government's efforts to rein in spending and cut debt could be faltering.\par \par \uc2 S&P\uc2  also downgraded, on Thursday afternoon, the ratings of many Brazilian companies, including state-owned oil driller \uc2 Petroleo Brasileiro SA\uc2 , whose shares closed 5% lower at 7.97 reais.\par \par \uc2 Other shares that declined include airline \uc2 Gol Linhas Aereas Inteligentes SA\uc2 , which fell 5.1% to 4.29 reais, and railroad operator Rumo Logistica Operadora Multimodal SA, which retreated 3.9% to 7.33 reais.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jeffrey T. Lewis at jeffrey.lewis@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 September 10, 2015 16:41 ET (20:41 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150910eb9a003ma\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
