\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Real leads Latam  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  gains as  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  steps up  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 469 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 September 2015\par 20:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SAO PAULO, Sept 8 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's real strengthened\par more than 1 percent on Tuesday, as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ramped up\par its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, while other\par Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose on a rally in Chinese stocks that\par fueled investors' appetite for risk globally.\par     The real was among the biggest gainers in Latin\par America as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  announced after markets closed last\par week that it would sell as much as $3 billion in the spot market\par on Tuesday through repurchase agreements.\par     Brazilian markets were closed on Monday for a national\par holiday. On Friday the real slumped more than 2.5 percent to its\par weakest level in 13 years, knocked down by fears of higher\par interest rates in the United States and by a political and\par economic crisis at home.\par     "Investors are relieved today thanks to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par dollar auctions and to international markets, with rising\par Chinese stocks," said Luiz Rugik, a trader with Correparti\par brokerage in Brazil. "But the short-term trend is still for a\par weaker real."\par     The Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has lost about a third of its value\par since the beginning of the year as a political crisis makes it\par more difficult for President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dilma Rousseff\f28 \uc2 \f2  to push through\par reforms needed to pull Latin America's largest economy back from\par a deep recession.\par     Concerns about the Chinese economy have also weighed on the\par real and other emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Tuesday's rally in Chinese stocks provided a respite,\par however, allowing the Mexican peso to gain 1.4 percent.\par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Colombia and Chile rose 0.9\par percent and 0.7 percent, respectively. \par     \par         \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1410 GMT:\par     \par  Stock indexes                    Latest       Daily  YTD pct\par                                                  pct   change\par                                               change  \par  MSCI Emerging Markets                791.7     1.74   -18.63\par  MSCI LatAm                        1,990.78     1.22    -27.9\par  Brazil Bovespa                   46,646.33     0.32    -6.72\par  Mexico IPC                       42,898.36     0.33    -0.57\par  Chile IPSA                         3,767.1    -0.21    -2.18\par  Chile IGPA                       18,406.45    -0.14    -2.46\par  Argentina MerVal                 11,129.56     1.84    29.73\par                                           9           \par  Colombia IGBC                     9,610.48     0.66   -17.40\par  Venezuela IBC                    14,771.54     0.25   282.81\par                                                              \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                           Latest    Daily  YTD pct\par                                                  pct   change\par     