\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  drop vs dollar; Brazil rate yields fall\b0\par\par\uc2 454 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juli 2015\par 19:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SAO PAULO, July 20 (Reuters) - Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par weakened on Monday, tracking the dollar's rally in global\par markets, while yields on Brazil interest rate futures dipped on\par the outlook for inflation.\par     Every major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the region eased against the dollar\par though Colombia's peso was little changed. Mexican \par and Chilean stocks moved slightly higher while Brazilian\par shares sank, driving the broader MSCI Latin American\par stock index to its second straight loss.\par     The dollar touched its highest since April 23 against a\par basket of major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , supported by statements made\par by Federal Reserve Chair \f28 \uc2 \f2 Janet Yellen\f28 \uc2 \f2  last week reiterating that\par U.S. interest rates will probably rise later in the year.\par     Mexico's peso weakened past the 16-per-dollar level\par for the first time despite recent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  efforts to\par support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  through market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Meanwhile, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's real  weakened for a third\par straight day as investors continued to weigh mounting political\par uncertainty due to conflicts within President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dilma Rousseff\f28 \uc2 \f2 's\par governing coalition. The infighting could potentially derail\par spending cuts critical to fending off a credit downgrade.\par     Yields on Brazilian interest rate futures <0#DIJ:> fell\par across the yield curve after a local news agency, citing "a\par qualified source," said the government is satisfied with what it\par sees as a decline in inflation expectations.\par     According to the results of a Reuters poll of analysts on\par Monday, Brazil's inflation rate likely slowed in the month to\par mid-July as the pace of economic growth has slowed, opening the\par door for a smaller interest rate hike later this month.\par  \par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1720 GMT:\par \par  Stock indexes                 Latest    Daily  YTD pct\par                                            pct   change\par                                         change  \par  MSCI Emerging Markets         934.47    -0.77    -1.53\par                                                 \par  MSCI LatAm                  2,426.18    -0.92   -10.23\par                                                 \par  Brazil Bovespa             51,819.92       -1     3.62\par  Mexico IPC                 45,593.09     0.59     5.67\par  Chile IPSA                   3918.15     0.46     1.74\par  Chile IGPA                 19,035.25     0.41     0.87\par  Argentina MerVal           12,183.85    -1.56    42.02\par  Colombia IGBC               9,989.33    -1.48   -14.14\par  Venezuela IBC              15,125.78     1.59   291.99\par                                                        \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest    Daily  YTD pct\par                                            pct   change\par                                         change  \par  Brazil real                   3.2148    -0.70   -17.34\par  Mexico peso                   15.997    -0.43    -7.83\par  Chile peso                    649.25    -0.54    -6.60\par  Colo