\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Pulls Back Further on  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\uc2  -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 615 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 2015\par 12:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 6:57 EDT - Following the Fed's latest statement yesterday, \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  took another step to reducing its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -swap contracts being offered through today's auction has been to cut to $260M from the recent $315M. Last week, \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced a size reduction for daily auctions. Since the start of this year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stopped offering new swap contracts and just offered certain ones to ensure market liquidity. \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts expect the gradual reduction of the daily auctions to continue the rest of 2015. (rogerio.jelmayer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 6:53 EDT - After visiting \uc2 Kohl's\uc2  (KSS) off-price test store in Cherry Hill, NJ, Sterne Agee doesn't see the department-store operator jumping with both feet into the space. Rather, the investment bank thinks "the concept is likely being viewed as an inventory-management tool and not a growth vehicle." Sterne Agee believes the effort "could be useful for KSS mainly as a 'loss-recovery' center in certain markets and view potential as mainly functional in nature." It calls store-traffic levels "decent despite low awareness levels," adding that "much of the product was \uc2 Kohl's\uc2  own brands," including Croft and Barrow, Jennifer Lopez, Apt. 9 and Juicy Couture. pressures or the relatively unconcerning DoJ investigation" into AMC and Regal (RGC) regarding competitive practices. (kevin.kingsbury@wsj.com; @kevinkingsbury)\par \par \uc2 6:35 EDT - AMC has the most \uc2 IMAX\uc2  screens of any US theater operator, and recent strong movie grosses for such showings--as well as improvements overall at the company's facilities--will help it show 2Q outperformance, says B Riley as it upgrades AMC to buy and ticks up its price target 5% to $35. The investment bank only left the bull camp barely 2 months ago, but since the stock has slid 18%. The drop "more than bak[es] in any potential risks around previously aggressive 2016 consensus estimates (they have since been pulled in), film-slate margin pressures or the relatively unconcerning DoJ investigation" into AMC and Regal (RGC) regarding competitive practices. AMC, inactive premarket, finished yesterday at $28.01. (kevin.kingsbury@wsj.com; @kevinkingsbury)\par \par \uc2 6:24 EDT - Offering a backhanded compliment to smaller and struggling rival Bombardier (BBD.B.T), \uc2 Airbus\uc2  (AIR.FR) chief salesman \uc2 John Leahy\uc2  says the Canadian firm has "a nice little airplane there," referring to the CSeries aircraft. He praised the jet's interior and its wider economy-class seats after touring it earlier this week at the Paris Air Show. But Leahy then immediately pivoted to smack chief rival \uc2 Boeing\uc2  (BA) on the width of its own economy-class seats and noted he saw BBD.B.T's new jet as no threat. (jon.ostrower@wsj.com; @jonostrower)\par \par \uc2 6:09 EDT - While there's been lots of M&A in healthcare of late involving publicly held companies on both sides, this morning brings a $510M buyout of laser-system maker Lumenis (LMNS) by investment firm XIO. Israel-based LMNS, which went public in the US in early 2014 at a less-than-expected $12, never caught investors' attention after the IPO either as have traded from $9-12. As such, the $14/share XIO has agreed to pay can be considered a nice win for investors. LMNS since the offering has remained dominated by a pair of pre-IPO investors; the investment firms owned a combined 77% before the company went public and still hold 59%. (kevin.kingsbury@wsj.com; @kevinkingsbury)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 18, 2015 06:57 ET (10:57 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150618eb6i0014u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
