\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Foreign Reserves Drop as  \highlight22\uc2 Interventions \highlight\uc2  Ease -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,497 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 April 2015\par 13:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 7:54 EDT - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves dropped in March, suggesting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reduced \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Reserves ended the month down $1.1B at $371.04B. Although the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't comment on its policy, some traders attributed the reserve drop to its lack of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. That may fall further as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week said it wouldn't renew its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap auction program. It expired Tuesday. (rogerio.jelmayer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1152 GMT Austria does not appear to be in a hurry to launch its first new government bond this year. At its next monthly bond auction on April 7, its Treasury taps September 2021- and March 2026-dated bonds, old paper that have already lost benchmark status and so aren't reopened on a regular basis any more. In fact, the two bonds were last auctioned in May 2011 and November 2011, respectively, note \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  strategists Alexander Aldinger and David Schnautz. Non-benchmark bonds are usually reopened either at dealers' requests or because the Treasury sees some price distortion on the yield curve due to reduced liquidity. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 7:51 EDT - Brazilian bankruptcy-protection filings rise in March hurt by a combination of a sluggish economy along with high interest rate and inflation, consumer credit-rating bureau Serasa Experian says. A total of 140 companies filed for bankruptcy-protection in March, up 6.1% from March 2014, according to Serasa. After expanding just 0.1% last year, Brazil's economy is expected to contract 1% this year, according to economists. (rogerio.jelmayer@wsj.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1141 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--The \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's asset purchases program will likely continue to strengthen the PLN and the HUF against the EUR throughout 2Q, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rabobank\f28 \uc2 \f2  strategist Piotr Matys. Says EUR/PLN is likely to break below the 4.05/4.00 support zone, which will expose 3.90/82 as the next potential mid-term target. As for the EUR/HUF, around 292 is the target. The fact EUR/HUF broke below the long-term upside trendline has strengthened Rabo's conviction that Hungarian assets will profit from the ECB's QE. As for risk factors, a collapse of the ceasefire in Ukraine's eastern regions would dent the positive view on the PLN and HUF, and Greece exiting the eurozone would trigger a painful squeeze on both \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Rabo adds. EUR/PLN is at 4.07, EUR/HUF is at 299.24. (margit.feher@wsj.com @margitfeher) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1131 GMT Hungary's 2014 budget numbers in its fiscal notification to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Commission\f28 \uc2 \f2  are encouraging, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  after the government says last year's budget deficit was 2.6% of GDP, less than the 2.9% goal and the EU's 3% tolerance threshold. Local governments reported an almost flat budget gap as a result of tighter controls on municipal budgets imposed by the central government a few years ago, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  says. "All in all a very positive development given how rating agencies and international institutions rate economic policy," it adds. Hungary is rated junk by all three main rating firms.(margit.feher@wsj.com @margitfeher) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 7:30 EDT - There's been a host of US economic data that's been meek of late, and if tomorrow's jobs report is the same, you can ice the potential of a mid-year FOMC rate hike. But don't overlook today's trade data for February. Further widening of the deficit could crimp estimates for 1Q GDP that much more, pushing them closer to zero. And regardless of the reason, if the US economy ended up contracting slightly last quarter, there's no way a majority of Fedsters would say yes to a rate hike in June. \f28 \uc2 \f2 S&P 500\f28 \uc2 \f2  futures are down 5.5 as gold edges lower and oil pulls back 3% after yesterday's bounce. The euro is stronger, rising to $1.0825, and Treasurys climb further, putting the 10-year yield at 1.84%. (kevin.kingsbury@wsj.com; @kevinkingsbury)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1116 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Hungary's local-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  government bonds are one of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2 's top trade recommendations due to their attractive valuation and the likelihood of credit-rating upgrades for the country, it says. Recommends an overweight position in the bonds. That view comes while \f28 \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2  has turned neutral on emerging-market local-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bonds due to concerns over \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  volatility and emerging-market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation. (margit.feher@wsj.com @margitfeher) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1051 GMT Investors' positioning in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets is light, with hedge funds and real money taking a step back from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bets after the high volatility seen in the first part of the year says BofA-\f28 \uc2 \f2 Merrill Lynch\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "Net long positioning is particularly low in Eastern Europe, ILS and TRY," says BofA, "while it has lately recovered in RUB and ZAR." Positioning is also light in bonds, except in Hungary and Poland. "Positions seem to have been reduced after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -led rally, but it remains most exposed in the case of a Greece-induced de-risking." (chiara.albanese@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1024 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--AUD/USD has just breached support at 0.7560, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays\f28 \uc2 \f2 , and is now on the way towards layered support between 0.75-0.7450. Below there the bank's longer-term target is the 0.71 area. AUD/USD is now at 0.7550, the lowest level seen since May 2009. (gary.stride@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1020 GMT Russia has been facing massive outflows of foreign direct investment from its stock market since March last year, the month when Moscow annexed Crimea. But now officials hope foreigners will be interested again in buying into Russia. The stock market has been falling for a while and one would be "a complete idiot" not to enter the market at some point, if sanctions do not restrict it, says Ruben Aganbegyan, head of Otrkitie Holding. The finance ministry agrees. As people realise Russia's economy is recovering, foreign investors will return, says Deputy Finance Minister Alexei Moiseev. The government expects the economy to start growing again as soon as 2016. Economists and global institutions, such as the \f28 \uc2 \f2 World Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 , are much less optimistic.(andrey.ostroukh@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1013 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--The June Bund future is putting pressure on resistance at 159.02, which is effectively the last line of defence protecting Wednesday's contract high at 159.21. Wednesday's push to 159.21 is part of a broader four-week advance from the base of an expanding bull pennant continuation pattern at 155.81, and the upward breach of 159.13 produced a new minimum upside requirement target at 159.73. The expanding pennant pattern's measured upside objective lands at 159.93, shy of the 160.00 all-time high that was traded on the continuation chart. The current session low at 158.74 marks an important support level for the near-term, guarding 158.63 and 158.48. The June Bund future is at 158.94. -By Francis Bray, Dow Jones Chief Technical Analyst For Europe.(francis.bray@dowjones.com) (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security or \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 . The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1012 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] India's finance minister Arun Jaitley said Thursday that the government wants to restore the credibility of the decision-making process and make the country's tax structure more taxpayer-friendly. "We're trying to restore the credibility of the Indian economy and the credibility of its decision-making process," Jaitley said at a conference in Mumbai. He added that the government is also trying to "rationalize the taxation structure" to make it "less adversarial." (gabriele.parussini@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 April 02, 2015 07:54 ET (11:54 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150402eb42001h7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
