\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Foreign Reserves Drop as  \highlight22\uc2 Interventions \highlight\uc2  Ease -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 933 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 April 2015\par 13:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 7:54 EDT - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves dropped in March, suggesting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reduced \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Reserves ended the month down $1.1B at $371.04B. Although the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't comment on its policy, some traders attributed the reserve drop to its lack of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. That may fall further as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week said it wouldn't renew its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap auction program. It expired Tuesday. (rogerio.jelmayer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 7:41 EDT - Susquehanna gets bullish on Dick's (DKS) ahead of the sporting-goods retailer's mid-month analyst gathering, hiking its price target $7 to $68 while upgrading the stock to positive. "We doubt management would plan an analyst day only to follow up with in-line or poor results a month later," the investment bank says. Combined with the event likely focusing attention on DKS' top- and bottom-line growth, "valuation remains attractive with shares trading in-line with its historical averages." DKS, which finished yesterday at $56.78 and is inactive premarket, has already climbed 14% this year. (kevin.kingsbury@wsj.com; @kevinkingsbury)\par \par \uc2 7:30 EDT - There's been a host of US economic data that's been meek of late, and if tomorrow's jobs report is the same, you can ice the potential of a mid-year FOMC rate hike. But don't overlook today's trade data for February. Further widening of the deficit could crimp estimates for 1Q GDP that much more, pushing them closer to zero. And regardless of the reason, if the US economy ended up contracting slightly last quarter, there's no way a majority of Fedsters would say yes to a rate hike in June. \uc2 S&P 500\uc2  futures are down 5.5 as gold edges lower and oil pulls back 3% after yesterday's bounce. The euro is stronger, rising to $1.0825, and Treasurys climb further, putting the 10-year yield at 1.84%. (kevin.kingsbury@wsj.com; @kevinkingsbury)\par \par \uc2 7:08 EDT - \uc2 Lumber Liquidators\uc2  (LL) says 1Q revenue growth was more than consensus estimates, which fell some 7% the past month in the wake of the "60 Minutes" report which raised potential regulatory and safety concerns. LL's revenue did slump 13% in March, with same-store sales down 18%. For the quarter, that metric fell 1.8%--though the number of customers rose 4.4%. While LL doesn't give a 1Q EPS forecast or indicate whether prior guidance on all of 2015 still stands, the flooring retailer does say the quarter's gross margin will be down some 5 percentage points from a year earlier. LL rises 2.2% premarket to $33.73 after already rebounding 8% this week. (kevin.kingsbury@wsj.com; @kevinkingsbury)\par \par \uc2 6:52 EDT - RBC has been saying Micron (MU) should build inventories in quarters of slower demand--often due to seasonal factors--as average selling prices are no longer falling 40-50% as they were for years during and after the financial crisis. So as the memory-chip maker plans to hold some near-term output, F3Q guidance late Wednesday was below consensus. But the investment bank says MU keeping product "should be viewed positively as it indicates strong demand in the back half of the year and more-stable pricing declines, which means holding inventory is not as costly and may serve the customer better in periods of demand exceeding supply." Shares are down 1.6% premarket at $26.70 despite its 2Q EPS beat. (kevin.kingsbury@wsj.com; @kevinkingsbury)\par \par \uc2 6:36 EDT - Canadian brokerage Canaccord (CF.T) which 2 months ago announced a 4% workforce reduction amid a soft capital-market environment, now has to navigate things without its CEO. Paul Reynolds has died in Hawaii "following complications related to a health incident while competing in a triathlon." The company on Monday said the 52-year-old was "hospitalized following an unexpected medical emergency during a family vacation. He remains in serious but improving condition." At the time, Chairman \uc2 David Kassie\uc2 --who will CF.T's new CEO--said Reynolds was "awake and responsive." Reynolds became the company's president in 2006 and CEO a year later and spent 3 decades with the firm. (kevin.kingsbury@wsj.com; @kevinkingsbury)\par \par \uc2 6:19 EDT - US stock-index futures are firmly in negative territory to start this final day of regular trading this week. Futures will trade for a bit after tomorrow's US jobs report, but stock exchanges will be dark for Good Friday. After starting the week with a sharp rebound following last week's pullback, the red returned the past 2 sessions, though a late rebound allowed the \uc2 S&P 500\uc2  to narrowly avoid finishing the day down for 2015; the \uc2 Dow\uc2  industrials is already there. \uc2 S&P\uc2  futures are down 8 points. (kevin.kingsbury@wsj.com; @kevinkingsbury)\par \par \uc2 6:14 EDT - China's efforts to stabilize its property market hasn't had much impact on the iron-ore market, with the benchmark price falling below $50/ton. Davy Research notes benchmark and premium prices are down 60% and 54% year-on-year, respectively. "Despite signs of stabilization emerging from the Chinese property market, overcapacity in the country's steel industry and the onslaught of global iron-ore supply growth are keeping sentiment firmly in bearish territory." (matthew.cowley@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 02, 2015 07:54 ET (11:54 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150402eb42001ek\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
