\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real drops as  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  ends  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 546 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2015\par 17:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par RIO DE JANEIRO, March 25 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real\par dropped more than 1 percent on Wednesday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par announced it will end its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  program at the end\par of March, reducing artificial support for one of the world's\par worst performing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The decision, in line with a broader government effort to\par reduce \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the economy, did not have an even bigger\par impact on the real because \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President Alexandre\par Tombini had already signaled the program could not be extended\par past March 31.  \par     The real lost 1.4 percent to 3.17 per dollar while\par other key Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  such as the Mexican peso\par  and the Chilean peso were steady or slightly\par stronger.\par     Expectation that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would scrap its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  program, combined with a growing economic and\par political crisis in Brazil and fears of higher U.S. interest\par rates, have driven the real nearly 16 percent lower this year.\par     In March alone, it has tumbled nearly 19 percent, which\par makes it the worst performer among the 152 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tracked by\par Reuters. \par     The real had been kept largely over valued during the past\par few years as President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dilma Rousseff\f28 \uc2 \f2  resorted to a number of\par unconventional policies to fight inflation. Since re-election to\par a second term in office starting this year, however, she has\par been trying to chance course.\par     Economists welcomed the end of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par program, which they said not only created economic distortions\par but had also become increasingly ineffective and expensive.\par     "A very welcome move and a step forward to facilitate the\par needed macroeconomic adjustment," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2 ' senior\par economist Alberto Ramos said in a note to clients. "In our\par assessment, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  excessively in the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market over the last 19 months."\par     Under the program, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  offered investors a\par daily supply of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swaps, derivatives that provide\par protection against \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  losses.\par     The stock of those swaps currently stands at around $113\par billion - an amount the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  considers enough to meet\par investors' demand for hedging. The bank said it will fully roll\par over swaps that mature on April 1 and beyond.\par \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1630 GMT\par     \par 