\par\par \b \uc2 A Tale of Two Europes: Germany Versus Greece -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 171 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2015\par 12:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 7:12 EDT - Markets are struggling with some competing signals out of the eurozone. On the one hand, Germany is booming--or so the latest business-sentiment data suggest. But on the other, the Greece problem is looking increasingly dicey as the ECB told the country's shaky banks to stop expanding their holdings of Greek sovereign debt. If it weren't for Greece, which is likely a factor in the weak trading so far seen in European equities, global investors would likely be in a better mood as a retraction in the dollar had helped to underscore a modest pickup in risk appetites. Shares in Asia and elsewhere were mostly buoyed overnight, and a surprise move by \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to end its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program didn't prompt any panic selling of the real or competing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (michael.casey@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (MORE TO FOLLOW) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 March 25, 2015 07:12 ET (11:12 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150325eb3p001ap\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Business\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Set To Reduce  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 77 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2015\par \uc2 RTT News\par \uc2 RTTNEW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2015 NoticiasFinancieras. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (RTTNews) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Tuesday it will not extend the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap program which is set to expire on March 31.\par \par \uc2 The program introduced in August 2013 provided protection against \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  losses.\par \par \uc2 The bank said it will conduct dollar auctions with repurchase agreements if it is needed to boost liquidity conditions.\par \par \uc2 For comments and feedback: contact editorial@rttnews.com\par \par \uc2 Copyright(c) 2015 RTTNews.com. All Rights Reserved\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTTNEW0020150325eb3p00235\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
