\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil real seesaws as cenbanker talks about swap plan\b0\par\par\uc2 404 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2015\par 20:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par RIO DE JANEIRO, March 24 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real\par swung widely on Tuesday as investors tried to decipher comments\par from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alexandre Tombini\f28 \uc2 \f2  about the future\par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  program.\par     The real rose more than 1 percent in the morning,\par initially boosted by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  decision to affirm\par Brazil's credit rating at BBB-minus with a stable outlook, a\par surprising vote of confidence in President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dilma Rousseff\f28 \uc2 \f2 's\par fiscal austerity policies. \par     It then erased all of the gains to drop nearly 1 percent\par after Tombini said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swap program has\par been an important tool to curb volatility in the real but\par already "substantially" meets investors' demand for hedging.\par     Some investors saw his remarks as a sign that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  intends to stop offering new swaps, which are derivatives\par that provide investors with protection against \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  losses,\par when the program expires in April.\par     Investors later turned more upbeat, however, when Tombini\par stressed that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is comfortable with the current\par stock of swaps and that it could roll over those contracts for\par many years to come. \par     The real last traded 0.4 percent stronger at 3.13 per\par dollar.\par \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1900 GMT\par     \par  Stock indexes       Latest       Daily  YTD pct\par                                     pct   change\par                                  change  \par  MSCI Emerging          979.13     0.38     1.99\par  Markets                                 \par  MSCI LatAm           2,496.65     0.04    -8.51\par                                          \par  Brazil Bovespa      51,091.61    -1.57     2.17\par                                          \par  Mexico IPC          44,043.42     0.21     2.08\par  Chile IPSA           3,893.49     0.39     1.10\par  Chile IGPA           18,981.9     0.41     0.59\par  Argentina MerVal    11,385.38     2.12    32.71\par                                          \par  Colombia IGBC        9,833.29     -0.8   -15.48\par                                          \par  Peru IGRA           12,532.58     0.06   -15.29\par  Venezuela IBC        4,796.18    -0.17    24.29\par                                          \par                                                 \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                      daily %    YTD %\par                                  change   change\par                         Latest           \par  Brazil real            3.1284     0.44   -15.05\par                                          \par  Mexico peso            14.907     0.13    -1.09\par  Chile peso             621.25     0.67    -2.39\par                                          \par  Colombia peso        2,510.57     1.97    -4.88\par                                          \par  Peru sol                3.066     0.26    -2.84\par  Argentina peso         8.7950     0.00    -2.79\par  (inte