\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real weakens to 10-year low on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  uncertainty\b0\par\par\uc2 462 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2015\par 22:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par RIO DE JANEIRO, March 3 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real\par closed at its weakest level in more than 10 years on Tuesday on\par concern about the country's deteriorating economic fundamentals\par and uncertainty about the future of a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  program.\par     The real has slid about 2 percent since the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  signaled on Friday that it would reduce the rollover pace\par of expiring \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swaps, derivatives that provide investors\par with hedge against \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  losses. \par     The move added uncertainty about the future of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  program, which is scheduled to\par continue at least until the end of March.\par     That leaves the real even more vulnerable to risks such as a\par sharp deterioration in economic fundamentals and the spillover\par of a growing corruption scandal at state-run oil company\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petrobras\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     "Brazil's economic and political situation is creating a lot\par of uncertainty among local and foreign investors," said Joao\par Paulo de Gracia Correa, a trader with Correparti brokerage in\par Brazil. \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petrobras\f28 \uc2 \f2 ' shares closed 2.1 percent higher, however, after\par the oil company more than doubled the amount of money it plans\par to raise through asset sales. \par     A source with direct knowledge of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petrobras\f28 \uc2 \f2 ' plan told\par Reuters that the company will focus on selling minority stakes\par as it seeks to retain control of its oil fields, power plants\par and utilities. \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petrobras\f28 \uc2 \f2 ' shares boosted Brazil's benchmark Bovespa index\par , which closed 0.6 percent higher. \par     In the opposite direction, Mexico's \f28 \uc2 \f2 IPC\f28 \uc2 \f2  stock index \par dropped 0.6 percent in its third consecutive session of losses\par on investor caution ahead of key U.S. economic data later in the\par week.  \par \par     Key Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and stock indexes at 2110 GMT\par     \par  Stock indexes                   daily %    YTD %\par                         Latest    change   change\par  MSCI Emerging           985.83    -0.25     3.34\par  Markets                                  \par  MSCI LatAm             2592.25    -0.86    -4.14\par                                           \par  Brazil Bovespa         51304.1     0.56     2.59\par                                           \par  Mexico \f28 \uc2 \f2 IPC\f28 \uc2 \f2             43600.37    -0.64     1.05\par                                           \par  Chile IPSA             3966.17     0.64     2.99\par                                           \par  Chile IGPA             19297.1     0.57     2.26\par                                           \par  Argentina MerVal      9682.109     1.11    12.86\par                                           \par  Colombia IGBC          10129.6    -1.61   -12.94\par                                           \par  Peru IGRA             13374.89    -0.34    -9.59\par                                           \par  Venezuela IBC          3751.39     0.49    -2.78\par                           