\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-\uc2 Brazil  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  taps Nomura economist for board\b0\par\par\uc2 450 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Februar 2015\par 23:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds comments, background)\par \par \uc2 By Flavia Bohone and Silvio Cascione\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/BRASILIA, Feb 5 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief, \uc2 Alexandre Tombini\uc2  , tapped a vocal critic to sit on the bank's board on Thursday, the latest effort by President \uc2 Dilma Rousseff\uc2  's government to win back skeptics in the financial markets.\par \par \uc2 Tombini nominated Tony Volpon, the head of emerging market research in the Americas for \uc2 Nomura Securities International\uc2  , as director of international affairs.\par \par \uc2 Volpon has criticized the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , called out Rousseff for profligate spending and argued against \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's use of capital controls. He warned as recently as October that a newly reelected Rousseff's honeymoon with markets could be "short and ultimately frustrating."\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is working to burnish its inflation-fighting credentials since an ill-fated effort to cut interest rates, starting in 2011, which fanned inflation without delivering the economic rebound promised by the government.\par \par \uc2 "There is little doubt that the policy experiment of 2011-2012 failed," Volpon wrote to clients a year ago.\par \par \uc2 "Unfortunately, the government engineered a massive loosening of fiscal policy and imposed capital controls in a bid to weaken (the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) ... Could anyone really be surprised that all that happened was higher inflation?"\par \par \uc2 Anchoring inflation expectations will be key for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it faces a series of price shocks this year from rising energy prices to concerns about power and water rationing.\par \par \uc2 Volpon would be the first \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  director to come from a private-sector finance job since \uc2 Aldo Luiz Mendes\uc2  joined the board in 2009, following a stint as chief financial officer of state-run \uc2 Banco do Brasil SA\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 Volpon's nomination drew immediate comparisons to Rousseff's surprise pick for finance minister in her second term. \uc2 Joaquim Levy\uc2  stepped down as head of asset management at \uc2 Banco Bradesco SA\uc2  to join the government last month.\par \par \uc2 "He is clearly a more hawkish voice for the board ... It brings someone from the market, from the private-sector like Levy," said Bruno Rovai, an economist with \uc2 Barclays\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 "But with so much bad news, I don't think this good news is going to bring much cheer to the market or take the premium out of the interest rate curve."\par \par \uc2 Volpon was one of two new directors Tombini suggested to Rousseff, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement on its website. He also nominated one of his own advisors, Otavio Ribeiro Damaso, to become director of regulation.\par \par \uc2 Both nominations must be formally approved by Rousseff and Brazil's senate. (Additional reporting by Brad Haynes. Editing by Andre Grenon) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-2-5T23:44:03.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150205eb2500vfm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
