\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Suggests Less  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  - -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,358 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Januar 2015\par 11:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 1003 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--The \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  implies reduced \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, after announcing earlier this week that it will continue to auction \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts until at least the end of March 31, 2015. It said that it will offer as much as $100 million in contracts in auctions held Monday through Friday. "The extension of 3 months is smaller than the previous extensions of the program (6 months) and the daily placements are also lower than the previous amount ($200 million per day)," noted economist team of Brazil's bank \uc2 Itau Unibanco\uc2  SA. (rogerio.jelmayer@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 1002 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--The second tenure of Brazil's President \uc2 Dilma Rousseff\uc2  started January 1, but the recovery of past economic resilience will take time, says \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2 ' Alberto Ramos. "Given the depth and breadth of the macro (economic) picture deterioration in recent years, it may take 2-3 years to repair the damage and recover the level of domestic and external resilience investors so highly valued in the not so distant past," he says. (rogerio.jelmayer@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0954 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Sterling falls to its lowest level against the dollar since August 2013, trading down to $1.5480 after the December Manufacturing PMI came in at 52.5 vs 53.9 forecast and 53.3 in November. Sterling also prints a fresh day low against the euro of 0.77865 from a six-year high of 0.7746 earlier in the day. (gary.stride@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0939 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Activity in the U.K.'s manufacturing sector grew at a slightly slower pace in December, in line with other indications that the broader economy is slowing. The manufacturing PMI fell to 52.5 from 53.3 in November, below the consensus forecast of 53.9. New orders slowed, and were largely driven by domestic contracts, while exports remained muted. Employment continued to rise, but with prices charged rising only slightly, the BOE is unlikely to be in any rush to raise its benchmark interest rate. (paul.hannon@wsj.com; Twitter: @PaulHannon29) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0933 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--\f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  yields move marginally higher in quiet European trade with limited data ahead to help provide direction. In the eurozone, peripheral bond markets continue to attract buyers, with Italy and Spain hitting fresh record yield lows, after ECB President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mario Draghi\f28 \uc2 \f2  told German daily Handelsblatt that interest rates are set to stay lower for longer. Ahead in the U.S., December ISM manufacturing and November construction spending. The March Treasury contract is 10/32 lower at 126-155 and the 10-year cash yields 2.205%. (nick.cawley@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0907 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--The eurozone's manufacturing PMI for December was revised down from the preliminary estimate, to 50.6 from 50.8. That still indicates that activity grew at a slightly faster pace than in November, but confirms that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  area's economy remained weak as 2014 drew to a close. Indeed, the PMIs for the fourth quarter were the weakest since the third quarter of 2013. New orders rose for the first time in four months, driven by export contracts, which suggests the euro's weakness may finally be providing some support to businesses. Manufacturers hire new workers, but they once again cut their prices, indicating the eurozone won't soon escape a period of very low inflation. (paul.hannon@wsj.com; Twitter: @PaulHannon29) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0856 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Activity in Italy's manufacturing sector suffered its sharpest contraction for 19 months in December, with the PMI falling to 48.4 from 49.0 in November, below the consensus forecast of 49.5. New orders also weakened, suggesting the sector won't soon return to significant growth, while manufacturers cut jobs for the fourth time in five months. They also cut their prices, as did French manufacturers. The manufacturing PMI for the eurozone's second-largest economy, France, was revised down to 47.5 from a flash estimate of 47.9, reaching a four-month low. (paul.hannon@wsj.com; Twitter: @PaulHannon29) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0843 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Indian technology company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cyient Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (532175.BY) Friday said it has signed a "definitive agreement" to buy a 74% stake in Rangsons Electronics Pvt. Ltd. It didn't disclose the value of the transaction, but said it would be an all-cash deal. Rangsons, based in the southern Indian city of Mysore, designs products for global companies in the defense, aerospace, medical, automotive, telecommunications and industrial sectors. The acquisition comes in the wake of the government's push to make the South Asian country a manufacturing hub, as well as create jobs for its semiskilled youth and narrow the trade deficit. (krishna.jai@wsj.com; Twitter: @jaikrishna) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: FLS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0833 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] While Kaisa Group (1638.HK) says it has defaulted on a US$52 million loan to \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2 , analysts say the company could still negotiate a delay on the payment. \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  asked for the cash back following the resignation late last month of the Chinese company's chairman \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kwok Ying Shing\f28 \uc2 \f2 . In a similar case late last year \f28 \uc2 \f2 Agile Property\f28 \uc2 \f2  (3383.HK) agreed with \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  and others to delay by a year a loan repayment. Some believe that option is also open to Kaisa. "The key thing is whether the company is able to negotiate a waiver with \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2 ," said Yin Chin Cheong, Chinese properties analyst at CreditSights. (enda.curran@wsj.com; Twitter: @endacurran) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0823 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Sweden's December purchasing manufacturing index for manufacturing comes in better than expected and brings hope for the sector's prospects, says Andreas Wallstrom at Nordea bank. PMI is 55.4 versus 52.7 in November and a Nordea forecast of 51. "The \f28 \uc2 \f2 first data\f28 \uc2 \f2  release of the year was indeed a positive one," Mr. Wallstrom says. Despite weak signals from trading partners, the situation in the manufacturing sector isn't that gloomy, he adds. Low interest rates and oil price will fuel the global economy, and in particular the manufacturing sector, throughout 2015, he says. EUR/SEK trades at 9.43. (charles.duxbury@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0821 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Spain's manufacturing sector grew at a slightly slower pace in December, with the PMI falling to 53.8 from an 89-month high of 54.7 in November. New orders also slowed, but employment continued to increase, with new hiring taking place at the fastest pace since June 2007. That suggests Spain's economic revival continued as 2014 drew to a close. (paul.hannon@wsj.com; Twitter: @PaulHannon29) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0805 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] India's imminent cellular frequency auction will be in focus in the first half of 2015, and "this can create some share price volatility depending on the final structure, terms and reserve prices," says Nomura. It adds that bidding for the frequencies by cellphone operators "could be more rational" in the upcoming auctions. The brokerage's note comes after the Indian telecoms regulator earlier this week set a starting price for frequency auctions, thereby kicking off this process. The government in February will auction off bandwidth frequency for third-generation, or 3G, cellular services. (krishna.jai@wsj.com; Twitter: @jaikrishna) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 02, 2015 05:03 ET (10:03 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150102eb12000n8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
