\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real rallies in thin trade as  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  eyed\b0\par\par\uc2 458 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 2014\par 14:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SAO PAULO, Dec 30 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real \par rallied on Tuesday, erasing the previous session's losses, with\par investors watching for an imminent announcement from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  over the future of its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  program.\par     Most other Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and stock markets edged\par higher.\par     The real strengthened nearly 1.8 percent, the most in nearly\par two weeks, partly due to traders seeking to move the so-called\par Ptax rate at the end of the month, which is used as a reference\par for a variety of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  contracts. \par     Trading volume was low in the year-end holiday period, with\par most market participants awaiting an announcement from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brazil's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  over expected modifications to its daily \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  program.\par     The bank has helped support the real by providing hedging\par protection to local businesses via \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swaps. It remains\par unclear how the program will be scaled down next year, and the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has said it would unveil its changes in coming\par days.\par     "You put together low liquidity, a fight over the end-month\par Ptax rate, and a lack of relevant news and the outcome is a very\par sensitive market," said Reginaldo Siaca, head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at\par brokerage Tov in Sao Paulo.\par     Brazil's benchmark Bovespa stock index rose for the\par fifth session in six, though gains were slight.\par     Shares of widely traded companies, such as lender \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banco\par Bradesco SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  and iron-ore mining firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vale SA\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par , contributed the most to the index's rise.\par     Should the Bovespa remain at its current level of 50,750\par points on Tuesday, it will close the year with a loss of about\par 1.5 percent. That move will be in line with predictions in a\par Reuters poll in September. \par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1324 GMT:\par     \par  Stock indexes                           daily %     YTD %\par                              Latest       change    change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets          954.75     -0.41     -4.39\par                                                   \par  MSCI LatAm                    2745.32       0.6    -14.75\par                                                   \par  Brazil Bovespa               50789.28      0.39     -1.39\par                                                   \par  Mexico IPC                          -         -         -\par                                                   \par  Chile IPSA                    3855.71      0.03      4.23\par                                                   \par  Chile IGPA                    18884.7      0.03      3.61\par                                                   \par  Argentina MerVal                    -         -   -100.00\par                                                   \par  Colombia IGBC                11570.54         0    -11.48\par                         