\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Brazil's Tombini warns inflation may accelerate in near term\b0\par\par\uc2 337 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Dezember 2014\par 17:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds details from hearing)\par \par \uc2 BRASILIA, Dec 9 (Reuters) - Brazilian inflation may accelerate further in the next few months, but policymakers will work to bring it back to target "as fast as possible," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Alexandre Tombini said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to lawmakers in Brasilia, Tombini said "it wouldn't be a surprise" if 12-month inflation shoots above current levels in the next couple of months as a weaker real boosts the price of imported goods.\par \par \uc2 He reiterated, however, that the bank remains committed to lowering inflation, currently hovering at 6.56 percent on an annual basis, to its 4.5 percent target.\par \par \uc2 "The timeline we are working with is the end of 2016," Tombini said.\par \par \uc2 Part of the decline in inflation is expected to come from a slower global economy and tighter fiscal controls in Brazil, he said, adding that the government's 1.2 percent primary surplus goal for 2015 should have a "neutral to slightly contractionary" effect on prices.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real, has weakened by more than 9 percent against the dollar this year as declining terms of trade and stronger U.S. economic growth sap demand for local assets.\par \par \uc2 Tombini said he does not see a need to unwind the bank's current stock of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps in the short term. The instruments are used to provide local businesses with hedging protection against \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves.\par \par \uc2 He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue to observe the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the next two weeks before deciding on the next steps for the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program.\par \par \uc2 Tombini said he expects a gradual recovery in \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy, which crawled out of a recession in the third quarter. A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  poll estimates the economy will grow 0.18 percent in 2014 and 0.73 percent in 2015. (Reporting by Luciana Otoni, Writing by Walter Brandimarte and Asher Levine; Editing by Alden Bentley and Paul Simao) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-12-9T17:11:28.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141209eac900izf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
