\par\par \b \uc2 Bank executive among finalists to be Brazil finance minister\b0\par\par\uc2 387 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 November 2014\par 16:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 SAO\uc2  PAULO/BRASILIA (Reuters) - Respected Brazilian banking executive Joaquim Levy is among three finalists to become the country's next finance minister, and President \uc2 Dilma Rousseff\uc2  could announce her pick later on Friday, a government official said.\par \par \uc2 Investors hope Rousseff will name a market-friendly figure such as Levy, who would signal a shift away from the leftist, \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies they blame for \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stagnant economic growth in recent years.\par \par \uc2 The other contenders are \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president \uc2 Alexandre Tombini\uc2  and \uc2 Nelson Barbosa\uc2 , a former number-two official at the finance ministry, the official said on condition of anonymity.\par \par \uc2 At this time, Rousseff favors leaving Tombini at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said another official close to the deliberations.\par \par \uc2 Levy is chief executive officer of Bradesco Asset Management, an arm of \uc2 Banco Bradesco SA\uc2 , the nation's second-largest private-sector bank. He was also the treasury chief during the first term of Rousseff's predecessor and political mentor, Luiz In\u225\'00\'E1cio Lula da Silva.\par \par \uc2 Levy was a last-minute addition to the race after his colleague Luiz Carlos Trabuco, \uc2 Banco Bradesco\uc2 's CEO, reportedly turned down the ministry job on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Still, Levy is widely respected among investors for being a fiscal conservative. Brazilian stock and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets rallied on Thursday on the chance that Rousseff will pick him for the job.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's benchmark Bovespa stock index surged 3 percent while Brazilian real gained nearly 2 percent.\par \par \uc2 "Levy is well known as an orthodox and pro-market policymaker who should help in the hard task of economic adjustment," Tony Volpon, head of emerging market research for \uc2 Nomura Securities\uc2 , wrote in a note to clients.\par \par \uc2 The University of Chicago-trained economist is considered a fiscal hawk who helped Brazil obtain its investment credit grade as treasury secretary, by keeping spending in check and overhauling its debt structure.\par \par \uc2 As minister, he would likely push for more transparency in fiscal accounts, which have deteriorated under Rousseff and raised the specter of a debt downgrade.\par \par \uc2 Tombini and Barbosa are both seen as more moderate than current Finance Minister Guido Mantega, but their appointment to the ministry would likely signal relative policy continuity.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Brian Winter and Luciana Otoni; Editing by Bernadette Baum and Nick Zieminski) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-11-21T15:28:25.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141121eabl00hd1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
