\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Markets End Mixed; Stocks Rise,  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Weakens\b0\par\par\uc2 By Paul Kiernan   \par \uc2 345 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 2014\par 21:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO--Brazilian financial markets were mixed at the end of trading Tuesday, as investors awaited the appointment of a new economic team by President \uc2 Dilma Rousseff\uc2  following her re-election last month.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark Ibovespa index of most-traded stocks closed 0.8% higher at 54383.59 points. Volume was moderate at 7.45 billion Brazilian reais ($3.1 billion).\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real weakened, however, and exited active trading at BRL2.5082 against the dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet, compared with BRL2.5021 at Monday's close.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to slightly reduce its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, rolling over only a part of the dollar-swap contracts it has expiring in December. The bank in recent years sold billions of dollars worth of swaps, which allow investors to hedge against future depreciation in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The market buys them because there's a scarcity of dollars," says Reginaldo Galhardo, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Sao Paulo's Treviso Corretora.\par \par \uc2 The rise in the stock market, meanwhile, came on the back of gains in banking, steel, food and beverage shares.\par \par \uc2 But two of the country's most important companies, mining giant Vale and state-owned energy firm \uc2 Petrobras\uc2 , posted losses. Vale shares tumbled 3.2% to close at BRL20.80 as prices for iron ore, its main source of revenue, declined. \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  shares ended 0.2% lower at BRL14.82 as investors remained skeptical of the company's chances of convincing Brazil's government to allow it to raise fuel prices at a board meeting in Brasilia on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 "Our stock market has entered a period of waiting for the names of cabinet members, and for important measures to guide a recovery of public accounts, reduce inflation and administer interest rates," Sao Paulo's SLW Corretora said in a monthly outlook.\par \par \uc2 Write to Paul Kiernan at paul.kiernan@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 04, 2014 15:20 ET (20:20 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141104eab4003v1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
