\par\par \b \uc2 RBCC- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Central Bk May Increase  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\uc2  -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,637 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 2014\par 12:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 1145 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--The Brazilian real's depreciation against the dollar is likely to force the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to increase \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, says Daniel Tenengauzer, \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2 . He also says the authorities are attempting to rein in inflation via monetary rather than fiscal means, but that they have not increased interest rates by enough to make much difference. RBC thinks \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have to increase its USD swap program to stop USD/BRL from overshooting. (rogerio.jelmayer@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 6:44 EST - Brazil's foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves increased $320M in October as investment values picked up, putting reserves--a significant part of the country's protection against global crises--at $376B. The increase came despite \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to avoid a sharp depreciation of the real last month. The biggest part of Brazil reserves are in US Treasurys, which rose in value amid broad gains in the global sovereign-debt market. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't comment on the performance of Brazil's foreign reserves. (rogerio.jelmayer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0000 GMT (\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 )--USD/CAD is probing above 1.1389 into levels last seen in July 2009, extending the powerful advance from the October 29 higher low at 1.1121. The strong rally from 1.1121 cements the bull flag continuation pattern that confined the setback to 1.1121 from the October 15 peak at 1.1389, and a broader-term 1.618 Fibonacci extension target lies at 1.1425. However, using the pivotal 1.06 level as a longer-term hinge, the peak of the long-term advance from the September 2012 base at 0.9632 indicates scope to 1.1795, coinciding with another 1.618 Fibonacci extension target. The 1.15/1.1525 area, incorporating the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level of the March 2009 to July 2011 decline from 1.3063 to 0.9405, would become the focus on a break above 1.1425. It would take a reversal below 1.1337 to defer the bullish outlook. USD/CAD is at 1.1393.\par \par \uc2 -By Francis Bray, \uc2 Dow Jones Chief Technical\uc2  Analyst For Europe.\par \par \uc2 (francis.bray@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security or \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 . The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 1117 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--Pressure on Hungary from the EU and the U.S. is likely to continue in 2015 as "the Orban administration has come under repeated external scrutiny due to its still rather cooperative stance toward Russia compared to most of its EU peers, and the administration's consolidated power relative to other parties," says analyst Raffaella Tenconi from \uc2 Bank of America Merrill Lynch\uc2 . The U.S. has put six Hungarian officials on a visa ban due to alleged corruption claims and the EU has harshly criticized Hungary's since then abandoned plan to tax Internet use. The pressure will likely "have a limited impact on Hungary's fundamentals" in 2015, Ms. Tenconi adds. (margit.feher@wsj.com @margitfeher) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1116 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--In a stark contrast with previous comments, the French finance minister launched a stern defense of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Tuesday. According to Mr. Sapin, the ECB is the only EU institution that has taken the right decisions to repair the suffering eurozone economy. The comments mark a change of position from August, when, in a radio interview, Mr. Sapin urged the ECB to implement decisions in order to bring the euro to a more "normal level." On Tuesday, Mr. Sapin also defended the ECB independence. "I'll repeat the rules: the ECB is independent and it is forbidden for anyone to put pressure on its decisions." Mr. Sapin also noted the independence of the ECB was inspired by the Bundesbank. "We must respect and apply the rules. I can even repeat that in German," he said, speaking in French. (william.horobin@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1110 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] RHB Research says the decline in crude oil prices is unlikely to derail Malaysia's goal to cut its fiscal deficit to 3.0% of gross domestic product in 2015. The house estimates that a decline of $10 per barrel in average crude oil prices will reduce government revenue by 4.0 billion ringgit. However, this will be mitigated by a corresponding reduction on the expenditure side through a lower fuel subsidy bill with a potential reduction of 2.5 billion ringgit in fuel subsidy for every $10 per barrel, RHB notes. The government derives about 30% of its revenue from the oil and gas sector and spent about 23.5 billion ringgit in 2013 on fuel subsidies. "We believe the government will be able to adjust its expenditure to make up for any shortfall in oil revenue caused by lower crude oil price," it adds. (jason.ng@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1101 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Hungary's 2015 budget assumptions are realistic and the draft budget reflects the government's responsiveness to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Commission\f28 \uc2 \f2 's requests for fiscal prudence, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of America Merrill Lynch\f28 \uc2 \f2  economist Raffaella Tenconi. The 2015 budget targets a deficit of 2.4% of GDP, instead of the 2.8% of GDP the EU expects for next year, and versus the 2.9% deficit the government forecasts for 2014. The 2015 budget is based on an inflation assumption of 1.8% and a GDP growth forecast of 2.5%. (margit.feher@wsj.com @margitfeher) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1100 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--German, UK and \f28 \uc2 \f2 US government\f28 \uc2 \f2  bonds all rose Tuesday after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Commission\f28 \uc2 \f2  cut its growth forecasts for the eurozone and the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 , fuelling hopes of lower rates for longer. December Bunds are 0.56 higher at 151.32, gilts are 0.54 higher at 115.37 and US Treasurys are 8/32 higher at 126-165. In the 10-year cash market, Bunds yield 0.812%, gilts 2.22% and USTs 2.32%, according to data from Tradeweb, all around 3-5bps lower on the day. The EC cut its 2014 eurozone growth forecast to 0.8% from 1.2% and slashed its 2015 forecast to 1.1% from a previous 1.7%. (nick.cawley@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1036 GMT \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of America Merrill Lynch\f28 \uc2 \f2  reckons the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hungarian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's bar is high for resuming its easing cycle and won't do so unless "the ECB gets it badly wrong". Hungary won't cut rates even if the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  revises \f28 \uc2 \f2 CPI\f28 \uc2 \f2  projections lower, for fear of a deterioration in investor sentiment as the FOMC rate hike approaches, says Raffaella Tenconi. Hungary extending last week its 'Funding for Growth' scheme until end-2015 "is effectively a new monetary stimulus," Ms. Tenconi adds. (margit.feher@wsj.com @margitfeher) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1031 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--After a fleeting small loss, EUR/USD is climbing despite the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Commission\f28 \uc2 \f2  slashing eurozone growth forecasts to 0.8% for 2014 and 1.1% for 2015, from +1.2% and +1.7% respectively. The Commission also cut its 2014 inflation forecast to +0.5% from +0.8%, and to +0.8% from +1.2% for 2015. EUR/USD now trades at 1.2522 from 1.2509 just before the event. (gary.stride@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1013 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The USD/PHP is a tad higher Tuesday, helped by the broadly bullish outlook for the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . "The dollar pierced 45 but there was strong selling pressure above that level. Banks are starting to take profit on the dollar. Long-term, however, the view still favors a stronger dollar," says a local bank trader. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pair settled at 44.915 after rising to an intraday high 45.05 and settling Monday at 44.90. Volume remains moderate. Traders expect the USD/PHP to stay within the 44.70-45.20 range in the near-term. (cris.larano@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1006 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Eurozone producer prices picked up in September, although that was almost entirely due to a rise in energy prices that is very unlikely to be sustained. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Eurostat\f28 \uc2 \f2  said producer prices rose 0.2% on the month, and were down 1.4% on the year. Economists had expected prices to be unchanged on the month. It was only the second month-to-month rise in prices this year, the last being in June. But excluding energy, producer prices fell 0.1% on the month, led by non-durable consumer and intermediate goods. So no relief for the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which likely faces many months of very low inflation. (Paul.hannon@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @PaulHannon29) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 November 04, 2014 06:45 ET (11:45 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141104eab4001lu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
