\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Foreign Reserves Up Despite  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 723 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 2014\par 12:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 6:44 EST - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves increased $320M in October as investment values picked up, putting reserves--a significant part of the country's protection against global crises--at $376B. The increase came despite \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to avoid a sharp depreciation of the real last month. The biggest part of Brazil reserves are in US Treasurys, which rose in value amid broad gains in the global sovereign-debt market. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't comment on the performance of Brazil's foreign reserves. (rogerio.jelmayer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 6:42 EST - \uc2 GM\uc2  is gaining ground in Brazil, one of company's most-important markets, due to its aggressive marketing campaign and a series of discounts. \uc2 GM\uc2  last month was No. 2 in sales, notching 19.1% market share. The second post is traditionally taken by \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  (VOW.XE), but the German auto maker has lost vigor in Brazil with the absence of new models in recent months. \uc2 Fiat\uc2  (FCAU) remains the market leader in Brazil. (rogerio.jelmayer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 6:39 EST - Weaker-than-expected 3Q results from US oil-drilling-equipment maker \uc2 Tesco\uc2  (TESO) as CEO \uc2 Julio Quintana\uc2  notes, "Managing exposure to various \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to be difficult in this economic environment. Also, as we tighten our credit policy in several international locations, deliveries of our products have a tendency to be pushed out into future quarters." But there are pockets of strength, with aftermarket sales and service revenue hitting a quarterly record TESO anticipates "very-strong delivery volume" this quarter. Shares, inactive premarket, fell 2.8% Monday to retrace some of the stock's recent rebound. (kevin.kingsbury@wsj.com; @kevinkingsbury)\par \par \uc2 6:28 EST - Weaker-than-expected 3Q revenue growth at \uc2 Vitamin Shoppe\uc2  (\uc2 VSI\uc2 ), helping cause the retailer's EPS to fall more than analysts anticipated amid a 2.7-percentage-point drop in gross margin amid the Nutri-Force acquisition as well as increased online sales and opening a new distribution center. But while rival \uc2 GNC\uc2  has been seeing same-store-sales declines, \uc2 VSI\uc2  logged 3.1% growth. The company, which now sees SSS growth at the low end of prior views and anticipates more growth on that basis in 2015, is inactive premarket after having pulled back 2.6% yesterday. (kevin.kingsbury@wsj.com; @kevinkingsbury)\par \par \uc2 6:19 EST - \uc2 Western Refining\uc2 's (WNR) 3Q profit surge was even bigger than Wall Street anticipated as the company benefited from robust margins thanks to "historical highs" in the WTI Midland/Cushing oil differential. While refinery production was flat, per-barrel gross margin surged to $24.04 from $14.22 at the El Paso and Gallup facilities. Last quarter may be as good as it gets for a while considering the narrowing of crude prices between the US and overseas amid the market's ongoing price slump. But investors have been optimistic that there's plenty of money to be made for now in refining. WNR, inactive premarket, is up 21% from last month's bottom. (kevin.kingsbury@wsj.com; @kevinkingsbury)\par \par \uc2 6:10 EST - Perhaps things are finally bottoming for Regis (RGS) as the salon operator logs slight same-store-sales growth following an extended stretch of declines, including the year-ago quarter's 5.4%. Nonetheless, the 1Q bottom line was weaker than a year earlier amid increased spending and staff incentives. CEO \uc2 Dan Hanrahan\uc2 , whose been trying to get things turned around during his 2-year tenure, notes "we continue to have a wide range of performance" among RGS' \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which include the Supercuts and SmartStyle chains. He adds "higher promotion levels and increased service-guest traffic" helped the quarter's results. Still, overall same-store customer levels fell 1.2% after last year's 7.2% slide. RGS, inactive premarket, fell 3.2% Monday following a sharp rebound the prior 2 weeks.(kevin.kingsbury@wsj.com; @kevinkingsbury) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par To contact the Market Talk Editors, \par Kevin Kingsbury, 212 416-2354, kevin.kingsbury@wsj.com \par Cynthia Lin, 212 416-4403, Cynthia.lin@wsj.com \par John Shipman, 212 416-2181, john.shipman@wsj.com \par Patrick Sullivan, 212 416-2326, Patrick.sullivan@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 November 04, 2014 06:44 ET (11:44 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141104eab4001mi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
