\par\par \b \uc2 PREVIEW-Brazilian steel eyes gloomy third quarter as demand falls\b0\par\par\uc2 641 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 2014\par 16:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SAO PAULO, Oct 27 (Reuters) - Brazilian steelmakers will\par likely report a second straight fall in profit in the third\par quarter, dragged lower by weak domestic demand from industrial\par consumers like the ailing auto industry.\par      Also weighing on the companies are falling iron ore prices\par which hit the mining units of the steelmakers.\par      Steelmakers Usiminas and CSN are\par expected to be the worst hit due to dependence on the Brazilian\par market. \par     Gerdau, on the other hand, is a stock more recommended by\par analysts due to its greater geographic spread and large\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the United States.  \par     Brazil's economy fell into a recession in the first half of\par the year undermining steel demand. \par     The industry had hoped this demand would pick up once the\par World Cup and related public holidays finished, but it continues\par to falter. In the auto sector, a major consumer of steel,\par production is down 16 percent so far this year with the industry\par forced to make hefty job cuts.\par     The iron ore price has also become problematic. \par     Brazilian mills invested heavily in recent years to install\par their own iron ore production, a tactic which both shielded them\par from rising prices of the steel-making ingredient and allowed\par them to benefit from the export of any surplus output. \par     But the iron ore price <.IO62-CNI=SI> has fallen 40 percent\par this year to near five-year lows. This has reduced profit from\par exports and undermined economic benefits of securing raw\par materials from their own mines.  \par      Widely diverse analyst forecasts all saw a drop in net\par income compared to the previous year at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Usinas Siderurgicas de\par Minas Gerais SA\f28 \uc2 \f2 , as Usiminas is formally called. Expectations\par varied from a hefty 177 million-real ($70.2 million) net loss to\par a slight 53 million-real profit according to five analysts.  \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cia Siderurgica Nacional SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  (CSN) is expected to post an 80\par percent drop in net profit compared with the same quarter last\par year.\par     In the case of Usiminas, the "average sales price is\par expected to decrease given poorer product mix and more exports,"\par Alex Hacking, analyst at Citi, said in a note to clients. "Iron\par ore results should fall 75 percent quarter on quarter on lower\par prices and volumes," he added.   \par     With weaker demand at home, Brazilian steel companies have\par been looking to export markets in order to keep mills running at\par high and efficient levels. But with an international surplus of\par the metal, prices are lower abroad than in Brazil, meaning\par margins suffer. \par       Steel companies also complain about the strength of\par Brazil's real  which reduces their\par competitiveness against international rivals.\par      Many economists calculate the real is overvalued given the\par country's economic situation with \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par regularly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prop up the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as a means of\par controlling inflation.  \par       \par  Average forecasts in Brazilian reais:\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 USIMINAS\f28 \uc2 \f2        Q3 2014*   Q3 2013    PCT change\par  Net income        ---       115 mln       ---\par  Net Revenue    2.909 bln    3.2 bln     -9.3 pct\par  EBITDA         398.4 mln    538 mln    -25.9 pct\par  EBITDA margin   13.5 pct     17 pct     -3.5 pps\par                                       \par  GERDAU                               \par  Net income       231 mln   642 mln       -64 pct\par  Net revenue    10.54 bln  10.5 bln      0.4 pct\par  EBITDA          1.17 bln    1.4 bln    -16.8 pct\par  EBITDA margin   11.2 pct   13.5 pct     -2.3 pps\par                                       \par  CSN**                                \par  Net income      85.5 mln    503 mln      -83 pct\par  Net revenue    3.945 bln  4.66 bln     -15.3 pct\par  EBITDA          1.17 bln  1.65 bln       -29 pct\par  EBITDA margin   29.7 pct     31 pct     -1.3 pps\par     *Analyst forecasts \par     **For CSN the averages are calculated using four forecasts,\par for the others five. \par   ($1 = 2.52 Brazilian reais)\par \par  (Reporting by Alberto Alerigi; additional reporting and writing\par by Stephen Eisenhammer Editing by W Simon)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-10-27T16:39:13.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141027eaar00ew8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
